 the default `tls.type: certManager` mode, cert-manager `Issuer` and CA `Certificate` resources and a chart-managed downstream `Certificate`; in the `tls.type: external` mode, a reference to your TLS Secret"},"375":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"cert-manager only for the default `tls.type: certManager` mode; for trusted TLS, a trusted issuer or a populated TLS Secret"},"376":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"Persistent application data"},"377":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"PersistentVolumeClaims required by the default local KMS and VA storage"},"378":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"A StorageClass, physical storage, backups and a shared/external backend when scaling requires one"},"379":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"Optional integrations"},"380":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"Configuration hooks for observability, AWS connectors and PKCS#11/HSM connectivity"},"381":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"The observability backends, cloud credentials and production HSM or external key service"},"382":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"The chart creates Lamassu's `Gateway` and routes. It does not install the Envoy Gateway controller or make the generated `LoadBalancer` Service reachable from your network."},"383":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"Use one Lamassu Gateway on ports 80 and 443 and let its HTTPRoutes dispatch traffic to every Lamassu service. Give that Gateway one externally reachable endpoint through the cluster load balancer, or forward traffic to it from an external proxy or NAT device. You do not need one Gateway per service."},"384":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#how-the-deployment-fits-together","content":"The chart creates one shared `Gateway` per Helm release. All chart-managed `HTTPRoute` resources attach to it. Envoy Gateway provisions the proxy data plane and a Kubernetes `LoadBalancer` Service for that Gateway."},"385":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#how-the-deployment-fits-together","content":"The `gateway.addresses` value is only an address request to the Gateway controller. It does not make an IP routable, open a firewall, configure DNS or create NAT. See Expose the Gateway before setting it."},"386":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#platform-requirements","content":"Kubernetes 1.24 or newer"},"387":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#platform-requirements","content":"Helm 3.2 or newer"},"388":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#platform-requirements","content":"Envoy Gateway 1.8 or newer and a `GatewayClass`"},"389":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#platform-requirements","content":"cert-manager 1.14 or newer; required only for the default `tls.type: certManager` TLS mode, not for `tls.type: external`"},"390":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#platform-requirements","content":"persistent storage suitable for the selected PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, VA and KMS configuration"},"391":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#platform-requirements","content":"a load-balancer implementation or another deliberate path from clients to the Gateway"},"392":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#platform-requirements","content":"KMS deployments using the native PKCS#11 sidecar require Kubernetes 1.29 or newer. Prebuilt Lamassu container images are published for `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64`, and the KMS PKCS#11 client module (`p11-kit-client.so`) is installed at the target architecture's Debian library path: `/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/pkcs11/p11-kit-client.so` on amd64 and `/usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/pkcs11/p11-kit-client.so` on arm64. The x86\\_64 path is retained as a compatibility alias for existing configurations."},"393":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#choose-the-next-page","content":"<Card title=\"Install with Helm\" description=\"Prepare dependencies, configure values, install and verify a controlled deployment.\" href=\"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm\" />"},"394":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#choose-the-next-page","content":"<Card title=\"Upgrade from 3.8.0\" description=\"Upgrade an existing Helm release to 4.0.0: architecture changes, breaking changes, migration steps and validation.\" href=\"/docs/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0\" />"},"395":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#choose-the-next-page","content":"<Card title=\"Expose the Gateway\" description=\"Choose an external traffic design, understand gateway.addresses and handle multiple Gateways.\" href=\"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking\" />"},"396":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/self-hosted/overview#choose-the-next-page","content":"<Card title=\"Use Fastlane\" description=\"Bootstrap a complete evaluation or lab environment with one script.\" href=\"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane\" />"},"397":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Deployment troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting"},"398":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","content":"Diagnose access, service health and infrastructure dependencies."},"399":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#diagnostic-sequence","content":"Diagnostic sequence"},"400":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#reproduce-a-single-operation","content":"Reproduce a single operation"},"401":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#separate-client-gateway-and-service","content":"Separate client, Gateway and service"},"402":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#review-kubernetes-status","content":"Review Kubernetes status"},"403":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#query-the-affected-service","content":"Query the affected service"},"404":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#validate-the-result-from-outside","content":"Validate the result from outside"},"405":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#minimal-evidence-collection","content":"Minimal evidence collection"},"406":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"I cannot sign in"},"407":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Everything returns 403 or 5xx"},"408":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#api-500-errors","content":"API 500 errors"},"409":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"A pod is not Ready"},"410":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"Events are not arriving"},"411":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#observability","content":"Observability"},"412":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","content":"Start by locating the failing layer. A Gateway response and an unready pod require different evidence. For rejected issuance or validation results, see PKI troubleshooting; for enrollment, see EST diagnostics."},"413":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#reproduce-a-single-operation","content":"Note the time in UTC, user or principal, resource, endpoint and result. Avoid repeating a destructive action such as revocation or deletion."},"414":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#separate-client-gateway-and-service","content":"Check the HTTP status. A 401 points to authentication; a 403, to authorization; a 404, to route or resource; a 5xx, to the service or a dependency."},"415":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#review-kubernetes-status","content":"Locate unready pods, restarts, recent events and the state of the release."},"416":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#query-the-affected-service","content":"Review its /health endpoint and its logs in the same time window. Then follow the indicated dependency: PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, the OIDC provider or the cryptographic engine."},"417":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#validate-the-result-from-outside","content":"For PKI, check the certificate, the chain, OCSP or CRL with the same type of client production uses."},"418":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#minimal-evidence-collection","content":"Replace the placeholders with your real release, namespace and deployment."},"419":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#minimal-evidence-collection","content":"Also run the chart's connectivity test:"},"420":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#minimal-evidence-collection","content":"The test checks the health of CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA, and verifies that the UI returns HTML. A passing test confirms basic connectivity, not a full issuance flow."},"421":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#minimal-evidence-collection","content":"The chart's services expose startup, readiness and liveness probes over /health. A pod can be running but receive no traffic if the readiness probe fails."},"422":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"If you receive a 401:"},"423":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"check that the UI's OIDC authority is reachable from the browser;"},"424":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"verify issuer, audience and expiration of the token;"},"425":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"confirm the Gateway can fetch the keys from the JWKS URI;"},"426":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"check that the provider's public and internal routes point to the same realm."},"427":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"If login succeeds but the APIs return 403:"},"428":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"inspect the token's real claims;"},"429":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"confirm they match an active principal;"},"430":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"review the policies granted to that principal;"},"431":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"verify that authz reaches PostgreSQL and its JWKS."},"432":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"On a fresh installation, confirm the migration Job finished. That Job creates schemas, migrates authz, preloads policies and provisions the principals defined in services.authz.bootstrap."},"433":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"External authorization fails closed by default. If authz is unavailable, protected routes are blocked."},"434":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Locate the authz pod and Service."},"435":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Check /health, logs and its database connection."},"436":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Verify the DNS and port configured in externalAuthorization."},"437":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Check the check route is /v1/ext\\_authz/check."},"438":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Do not switch to failOpen: true as a permanent workaround: it would allow traffic without authorization during the outage."},"439":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#api-500-errors","content":"A 500 indicates an internal failure, such as an unavailable database. The `{\"err\": ...}` body currently includes the text of the internal error, which can contain schema, table and constraint names and, on connection failures, the database host and user (not the password). Find the cause in the service log using the request time, and do not forward the body to third parties or show it to end users. This is a known information-disclosure defect: generic messages are planned for 500 responses, keeping the detail only in the service log (tracked in lamassuiot#814). The authorization connector also returns the internal error, in the `details.error` field. Some request errors, such as a key size the engine does not support, are also returned as 500."},"440":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"Review kubectl describe pod first. Common causes are:"},"441":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"wrong credentials or DNS for PostgreSQL or RabbitMQ;"},"442":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"a missing AMQP CA or client certificate Secret referenced by `amqp.ca.secretName` or `amqp.client.secretName`;"},"443":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"unbound persistent volume;"},"444":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"inaccessible image or incorrect pull policy;"},"445":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"invalid cryptographic engine configuration;"},"446":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"CPU or memory limits set too low;"},"447":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"an incomplete prior migration."},"448":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"Generic values request 100 mCPU and 128 MiB and limit to 500 mCPU and 512 MiB. Tune per service when you see OOMKills, throttling or slow startups."},"449":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"Filesystem-based KMS engines and VA local storage use exclusive-access volumes. Keep a single replica or migrate to shared backends before enabling autoscaling."},"450":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"Internal calls now fail fast instead of hanging for the clients covered by Egress proxy: connection attempts time out after 30 seconds and TLS handshakes after 10 seconds. The authorization-engine connector keeps its own transport without these dial and handshake timeouts; only its overall 30-second request timeout bounds each call. If an egress proxy handles the cluster's outbound traffic, check the pod's `HTTP_PROXY`, `HTTPS_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY` environment variables and list in-cluster service names in `NO_PROXY`."},"451":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"Domain and audit events depend on the bus publisher:"},"452":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"verify it is enabled in the emitting service;"},"453":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"check AMQP connectivity and credentials;"},"454":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"review exchange, routing key, queues and consumers;"},"455":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"inspect dead-letter queues;"},"456":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"alert on orphan durable queues and backlog growth."},"457":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"If `amqp.tls` is enabled, verify the TLS side as well:"},"458":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"confirm the broker listener speaks AMQPS on the configured port — the default port stays `5672` and does not follow TLS automatically;"},"459":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"if you set `amqp.ca.secretName`, confirm the Secret exists in the release namespace and its data key matches `amqp.ca.certificateKey` (default `ca.crt`); if `amqp.ca.secretName` is not set, the clients trust the system CAs;"},"460":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"remember that a missing referenced Secret prevents the consuming pods from starting;"},"461":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"after updating the CA or client certificate Secret, restart the consuming pods: the AMQP client loads certificates at startup."},"462":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"See AMQP TLS (AMQPS) for the full configuration."},"463":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"A consumer outage does not always prevent the main operation from completing. That is why you must monitor RabbitMQ and independently verify the persistence of audit logs."},"464":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#observability","content":"The chart can enable OpenTelemetry instrumentation for the services that support it, including authz; it does not configure OpenTelemetry for AWS Connector, wfx or the UI. Traces are exported over OTLP HTTP and logs can be directed to a compatible endpoint, such as VictoriaLogs. Use a correlation identifier and the same time window to join Gateway, service and dependency."},"465":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#observability","content":"Before closing an incident, record:"},"466":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#observability","content":"the confirmed cause;"},"467":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#observability","content":"the time scope and affected resources;"},"468":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#observability","content":"the commands or queries used;"},"469":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#observability","content":"the applied change and how to revert it;"},"470":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#observability","content":"validation from a consumer;"},"471":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/deployment/troubleshooting#observability","content":"the preventive action and its owner."},"472":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"page","content":"Access control","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Administration"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control"},"473":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","content":"Design who can access Lamassu through principals, policies, resource permissions and HTTP route authorization."},"474":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#essential-concepts","content":"Essential concepts"},"475":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#two-decision-systems","content":"Two decision systems"},"476":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"Integrated or external HTTP services"},"477":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#authentication-only-routes-and-unmapped-paths","content":"Authentication-only routes and unmapped paths"},"478":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"Services developed by Lamassu"},"479":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#how-the-two-paths-relate","content":"How the two paths relate"},"480":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#oidc-principals","content":"OIDC principals"},"481":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#x509-principals","content":"X.509 principals"},"482":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#when-several-principals-match","content":"When several principals match"},"483":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#how-policies-express-access","content":"How policies express access"},"484":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#global-and-direct-access","content":"Global and direct access"},"485":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#access-inherited-through-relations","content":"Access inherited through relations"},"486":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#attribute-filtered-access","content":"Attribute-filtered access"},"487":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#http-rules","content":"HTTP rules"},"488":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#included-policies","content":"Included policies"},"489":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"Provision the first administrator"},"490":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#prepare-the-identity-provider","content":"Prepare the identity provider"},"491":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#configure-token-validation","content":"Configure token validation"},"492":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#install-and-verify-administrative-access","content":"Install and verify administrative access"},"493":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#test-an-unprivileged-identity","content":"Test an unprivileged identity"},"494":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#reduce-use-of-the-bootstrap-administrator","content":"Reduce use of the bootstrap administrator"},"495":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#fastlane-bootstrap","content":"Fastlane bootstrap"},"496":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#design-least-privilege-roles","content":"Design least-privilege roles"},"497":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#changes-and-access-revocation","content":"Changes and access revocation"},"498":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#operational-checklist","content":"Operational checklist"},"499":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#diagnostics","content":"Diagnostics"},"500":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#the-response-is-401","content":"The response is 401"},"501":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#the-response-is-403","content":"The response is 403"},"502":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#everything-returns-403","content":"Everything returns 403"},"503":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#access-appears-without-a-policy-grant","content":"Access appears without a policy grant"},"504":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#everything-fails-when-authz-is-unavailable","content":"Everything fails when authz is unavailable"},"505":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","content":"Lamassu access control turns an authenticated identity into concrete permissions. The OIDC provider or the client certificate proves **who** makes a request; the `authz` service decides **what that identity can do** and **over which resources**."},"506":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","content":"Lamassu does not assign permissions directly to users. The full chain is:"},"507":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","content":"This model lets you represent people, identity-provider groups, service accounts and devices without coupling authorization to a specific provider."},"508":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#essential-concepts","content":"A **principal** connects a credential to Lamassu. It defines how to recognize an OIDC or X.509 identity and can be active or disabled."},"509":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#essential-concepts","content":"A **policy** groups reusable permissions. It can be granted to several principals and can contain rules about Lamassu entities, rules about HTTP routes or both."},"510":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#essential-concepts","content":"An **entity rule** grants actions over resources such as certification authorities, certificates, issuance profiles, devices, DMSs, keys or alert subscriptions. It can cover all resources of a type or be limited by identifier, relation or attribute."},"511":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#essential-concepts","content":"An **HTTP rule** grants actions associated with API routes. It is the mechanism the Gateway uses to decide whether a request may cross the perimeter."},"512":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#essential-concepts","content":"A **grant** is the association between a principal and a policy. Removing the grant removes all permissions contributed by that policy, without modifying it for other principals."},"513":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#essential-concepts","content":"A valid JWT or a valid client certificate does not grant access by itself. The credential must match at least one active principal and, unless the HTTP schema exempts the route, one of its policies must allow the requested operation. See *Authentication-only routes and unmapped paths* for those exemptions."},"514":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#two-decision-systems","content":"Lamassu uses two authorization paths depending on who implements the protected service. They share principals, policies and grants, but they do not interpret the rules the same way."},"515":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#two-decision-systems","content":"An external service can be protected without knowing Lamassu's internal authorization model. A service developed by Lamassu embeds the authorization engine and can decide on concrete resources and filter its queries."},"516":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"This path protects APIs that join the platform through the Gateway but do not natively implement Lamassu's authorization SDK. Job Manager is the current example. The same pattern allows integrating other HTTP services as long as their routes are described in an `authz` HTTP schema."},"517":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"The decision is made **before forwarding the request to the service**:"},"518":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"Envoy Gateway authenticates the request, usually validating a JWT against the OIDC provider's JWKS."},"519":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"For a protected route, Envoy sends the method, URL, headers and required data to `/v1/ext_authz/check`."},"520":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"`authz` extracts the credential and resolves all active principals matching it."},"521":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"It separately loads the policies granted to each principal."},"522":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"The HTTP schema translates the method and route combination into a logical action, such as `nbi-job-read` or `nbi-workflow-create`."},"523":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"`authz` looks for an HTTP rule granting that action."},"524":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"If the route declares constraints, it compares request data with the normalized attributes of the same principal contributing the policy; the policy's own `param_constraints` also pin the granted action to literal request values."},"525":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"A satisfying result lets Envoy forward the request; any other response blocks it at the Gateway."},"526":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"When it allows access, `authz` returns the selected principal in the `X-Principal-ID` response header. The Gateway can propagate that header to the service to preserve the identity context. Clients cannot forge this header: the Gateway removes client-supplied `X-Principal-Id` (and the other forwarded identity and certificate headers) before forwarding, so only `authz` can set it. See Expose the Gateway for the full list of stripped headers."},"527":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#integrated-or-external-http-services","content":"HTTP rules primarily answer &#x2A;*\"can this identity call this API operation?\"**. On their own they do not produce filters over the external service's database. To limit a route to a specific device, tenant or client, either the schema declares a constraint relating a request value to a normalized attribute of the principal, or the policy pins the request value to a literal with `param_constraints`. The first scopes each identity to its own resources through a single grant; the second restricts a grant to a fixed value regardless of who holds it."},"528":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#authentication-only-routes-and-unmapped-paths","content":"Two schema-level settings cover endpoints that policies do not mention:"},"529":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#authentication-only-routes-and-unmapped-paths","content":"**`skip_authz: true` on a route** allows any identity that matches an active principal to reach it, even one with no granted policies. Use it for paths such as `/openapi.json` or `/health` that every authenticated caller should be able to access. The request still has to authenticate successfully: a credential that fails validation or matches no active principal is rejected before this setting is considered. A `skip_authz` route cannot declare constraints, and it wins over any other schema's route or default action for the same request."},"530":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#authentication-only-routes-and-unmapped-paths","content":"**`default_action` with `base_paths`** decides what happens when a request falls under a path prefix the schema owns but no explicit route matches. `deny` — the value the Job Manager schema ships with — turns the implicit denial of unmapped paths into an explicit, auditable statement; `allow` opens unmapped endpoints under that prefix to any identity that matches an active principal."},"531":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#authentication-only-routes-and-unmapped-paths","content":"These are decisions of the schema, not of a policy: `skip_authz` removes the grant check for that route, even when another schema maps the same request to an action that requires a grant, and `default_action` only covers requests that no explicit route in any schema matches. Keep three rules in mind:"},"532":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#authentication-only-routes-and-unmapped-paths","content":"`default_action` requires at least one `base_paths` entry, and base paths are absolute paths such as `/api/wfx/nbi/v1`."},"533":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#authentication-only-routes-and-unmapped-paths","content":"An explicit route in any schema takes precedence: the fallback only decides requests that no schema's routes cover. When the prefixes of two schemas overlap, the longest matching prefix decides."},"534":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#authentication-only-routes-and-unmapped-paths","content":"Two schemas cannot claim the same base path with different default actions; the conflicting schema fails to load."},"535":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#authentication-only-routes-and-unmapped-paths","content":"A `skip_authz` route and a `default_action: \"allow\"` prefix grant access without consulting any policy. Every identity that matches an active principal can reach what they open, including identities with no granted policies. A `skip_authz` route in one schema also opens a request that another schema maps to a grant-protected action. Review these settings whenever you add or upgrade an integrated service."},"536":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"Lamassu's native services embed authorization in their middleware and know the entities they operate on: certificates, CAs, issuance profiles, keys, devices, DMSs or subscriptions, among others."},"537":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"The decision is made with the domain operation context:"},"538":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"The middleware extracts the credential and resolves the matching principals."},"539":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"The endpoint identifies the action, the entity type and, when applicable, the key of the requested resource."},"540":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"`authz` gathers the entity rules of the granted policies."},"541":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"The engine evaluates direct grants, attribute filters and relations with other entities."},"542":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"For an individual operation, it checks that the concrete resource satisfies the computed scope."},"543":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"For a listing, it generates a SQL filter that the service adds to its own query."},"544":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"Here the engine answers &#x2A;*\"can this identity perform this action on this concrete resource?\"**."},"545":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"Actions fall into two groups:"},"546":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"**Global actions** do not need a resource identifier. `create`, `import` or access to a console section are common examples."},"547":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"**Atomic actions** are evaluated on a concrete instance. For certificates these include `read`, `metadata-update`, `status-update` and `delete`; for a CA there are also `sign`, `reissue` and other lifecycle operations."},"548":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#services-developed-by-lamassu","content":"Filtering inside the service prevents leaks in listings: unauthorized resources are excluded from the SQL query instead of being fetched and hidden later in the interface."},"549":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#how-the-two-paths-relate","content":"They are not two equivalent controls applied twice. HTTP rules protect the perimeter of an integrated service; entity rules express permissions over the data model of the native services."},"550":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-77","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#how-the-two-paths-relate","content":"A policy can contain both rule types when an identity needs to operate Lamassu resources and also call an integrated API. Granting an entity rule does not automatically grant an HTTP action, nor does an HTTP rule create access over an entity."},"551":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-78","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#how-the-two-paths-relate","content":"If no combination of principal, policy and rule allows the operation, Lamassu denies it, unless the HTTP schema declares `skip_authz` on the route or `default_action: allow` on a base path that covers it (see *Authentication-only routes and unmapped paths*). Additionally, `auth.externalAuthorization.failOpen` is `false` by default: if `authz` is unavailable, the Gateway blocks protected routes."},"552":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-79","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#oidc-principals","content":"An OIDC principal matches the claims of a validated JWT. It is appropriate for human users, corporate groups, IdP roles and service accounts that obtain tokens."},"553":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-80","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#oidc-principals","content":"The following principal represents any identity holding the `pki-operators` role in Keycloak:"},"554":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-81","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#oidc-principals","content":"Claim paths can be nested, such as `realm_access.roles`. Within a single principal, **all** conditions must hold. This lets you require, for example, a group and an organizational audience at the same time."},"555":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-82","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#oidc-principals","content":"The implemented operators are:"},"556":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-83","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#oidc-principals","content":"`equals`, for exact equality;"},"557":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-84","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#oidc-principals","content":"`contains`, to check membership in a list or the presence of text in a scalar value."},"558":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-85","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#oidc-principals","content":"Design matching with stable attributes. For people, it is usually better to bind permissions to centrally managed groups or roles than to the email or username. For a service account, a stable `sub` keeps its permissions from mixing with a human operator's."},"559":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-86","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#oidc-principals","content":"Although the model recognizes the operator name `matches`, the current implementation does not evaluate regular expressions and the condition never matches. Use `equals` or `contains`."},"560":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-87","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#x509-principals","content":"An X.509 principal lets you recognize a workload or a device by its client certificate. Lamassu checks the certificate signature against the configured CA and, depending on the mode, also its serial number or Common Name."},"561":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-88","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#x509-principals","content":"The available modes are:"},"562":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-89","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#x509-principals","content":"`serial_and_ca`: an exact certificate, identified by serial number and CA;"},"563":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-90","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#x509-principals","content":"`cn_and_ca`: an exact or wildcard Common Name and a specific CA;"},"564":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-91","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#x509-principals","content":"`any_from_ca`: any certificate issued directly by the given CA."},"565":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-92","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#x509-principals","content":"This example recognizes certificates whose CN starts with `factory-a-` and that are signed by the configured CA:"},"566":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-93","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#x509-principals","content":"`ca_trust.identity_type` accepts `fingerprint` or `authority_key_id`. In both cases you must provide the CA certificate in `ca_trust.pem`; Lamassu verifies both the signature and the expected identity of the CA."},"567":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-94","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#x509-principals","content":"Use `any_from_ca` only when every identity issued by that CA should share the same permissions. If a CA issues certificates for different populations, separate access by serial or CN, or use different issuing CAs."},"568":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-95","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#when-several-principals-match","content":"A single credential can match more than one principal. It is common for a user to match a principal of their team and another of their operational function."},"569":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-96","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#when-several-principals-match","content":"For entity permissions, Lamassu combines permissions with OR logic: it is enough that one policy of one of the principals allows the action. Listings contain the union of the resources visible to all of them."},"570":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-97","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#when-several-principals-match","content":"HTTP routes with constraints are stricter. The same principal contributing the policy must also satisfy the attributes required by the route. Lamassu does not combine one principal's policy with an attribute belonging to another."},"571":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-98","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#when-several-principals-match","content":"For this reason, adding a matching principal can only broaden access. Before creating overlapping rules, review the full set of policies a real identity will receive."},"572":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-99","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#global-and-direct-access","content":"A rule identifies the domain (`namespace`), the data schema (`schema_name`) and the entity type (`entity_type`). `actions` lists the allowed operations."},"573":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-100","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#global-and-direct-access","content":"`direct_grants` limits the rule to concrete identifiers. The value `*` covers all instances of the type. A superadministrator policy uses wildcards in schema, entity, actions and grants; a least-privilege policy should avoid them whenever possible."},"574":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-101","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#access-inherited-through-relations","content":"Rules can follow relations declared between entities. For example, the schema knows the relation of a certificate to its issuing CA, of a device to its DMS and of a certificate to the KMS key that stores its private key, so a grant on the key also covers the certificates that use it. A policy can grant access to a parent resource and propagate selected actions to its related resources."},"575":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-102","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#access-inherited-through-relations","content":"This lets you express models like \"can operate the devices of this DMS\" without maintaining an individual list of every device. When a resource is added under that relation, it inherits the scope planned by the policy."},"576":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-103","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#attribute-filtered-access","content":"`column_filters` applies conditions to columns the schema has declared filterable. All filters of the same rule are combined with AND."},"577":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-104","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#attribute-filtered-access","content":"For example, this rule allows reading active certificates issued by a specific CA:"},"578":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-105","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#attribute-filtered-access","content":"The available operators are `eq`, `neq`, `gt`, `gte`, `lt`, `lte`, `in` and `like`. Use comparisons consistent with the column type: `like` for text, ordering comparisons for numbers or dates and `in` when there is a collection of accepted values."},"579":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-106","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#http-rules","content":"HTTP rules do not point directly at tables. They reference a route schema and grant its logical actions. Job Manager's policies are an example: they distinguish reading, creating, updating and deleting workflows or jobs."},"580":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-107","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#http-rules","content":"Some routes also compare a request value — taken from the path, query, header or JSON body — with a normalized attribute of the principal. This way you can verify that a device only queries jobs addressed to its own `client_id`."},"581":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-108","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#http-rules","content":"Normalized attributes decouple the policy from the authentication mechanism. `subject_attribute_mappings` can derive, for example, `device_id` from `oidc.claim.device_id` or from `x509.subject.cn`. The rule consumes `device_id` in both cases."},"582":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-109","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#http-rules","content":"An HTTP rule can also pin a granted action to a literal value carried by the request itself through `param_constraints`. It extracts the value with the same sources as route constraints — `path_regex_group`, `query`, `header` or `json_body` — but compares it against an `equals` literal written into the policy rather than against a subject attribute. The grant then depends only on the request, not on who holds the policy:"},"583":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-110","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#http-rules","content":"Combined with a schema route such as `^/api/mysvc/system/([^/]+)/info$`, this grants `GET /api/mysvc/system/1/info` and denies the same call for system `2`, regardless of the principal's attributes. The same mechanism pins query parameters, headers or JSON body fields, for example `{ \"source\": \"query\", \"name\": \"tenant_id\" }` with `\"equals\": \"1\"` to accept only requests carrying `?tenant_id=1`."},"584":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-111","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#http-rules","content":"Note that:"},"585":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-112","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#http-rules","content":"`action` must be one of the actions granted by the rule; `equals` is required; `path_regex_group` needs an `index` greater than zero, `query` and `header` need a `name`, and `json_body` needs a `path` such as `$.tenant_id`."},"586":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-113","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#http-rules","content":"`param_constraints` are not cross-checked against the schema when the policy is loaded. A reference the route cannot satisfy — for instance a `path_regex_group` on a route without capture groups — simply never matches, and the request is denied."},"587":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-114","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#http-rules","content":"Several `param_constraints` for the same action combine with AND. A rule without them keeps the usual behavior: the action is granted wherever the route matches and the subject constraints pass."},"588":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-115","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#included-policies","content":"The `authz` preload installs reusable policies for the main domains. Among them are:"},"589":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-116","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#included-policies","content":"full and read-only access to certificates and authorities;"},"590":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-117","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#included-policies","content":"full and read-only access to the KMS;"},"591":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-118","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#included-policies","content":"full and read-only access to Device Manager, DMS Manager, Validation Authority and alerts;"},"592":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-119","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#included-policies","content":"an `Auditor` policy with PKI read access and authorization visibility;"},"593":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-120","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#included-policies","content":"console access;"},"594":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-121","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#included-policies","content":"administration and observation policies for the Job Manager NBI and SBI APIs;"},"595":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-122","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#included-policies","content":"`SUPER ADMIN`, which grants all actions over the `authz` and `pki` domains."},"596":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-123","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#included-policies","content":"Start with these policies before creating others. If none reflects the boundary you need, create a specific, small policy instead of copying `SUPER ADMIN` and informally removing permissions."},"597":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-124","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"An installation without a principal matching your identity is left with nobody able to administer authorization. Configure the IdP and the bootstrap before exposing the platform."},"598":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-125","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"The chart includes a bootstrap principal that looks for the OIDC role `pki-admin` in `realm_access.roles`. It grants it `SUPER ADMIN` and, when Job Manager is enabled, the administrative policy of its NBI API."},"599":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-126","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"The pre-install and pre-upgrade Helm Job runs the `authz` migrations, preloads the policies and creates the bootstrap principals before the services start. If the principal already exists, it does not replace it: it only adds the configured grants that are still missing. You can keep the entry in `values.yaml` across upgrades."},"600":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-127","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#prepare-the-identity-provider","content":"Create the role or group you will use to administer Lamassu. Assign it to at least two controlled human identities. If your provider does not use `realm_access.roles`, adapt the claim path in both the frontend and `auth_config.claims`."},"601":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-128","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#configure-token-validation","content":"`authz` validates every token against `services.authz.jwkUrl`, which is fetched from the `authz` pod. The Gateway does not validate tokens itself: Lamassu services authorize each request through `authz`, and routes labeled `auth=external`, such as the Job Manager ones, are checked by the Gateway through `authz` when `auth.externalAuthorization` is enabled. The endpoint must serve the keys of the issuer configured in `auth.oidc.frontend.authority`."},"602":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-129","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#configure-token-validation","content":"Releases upgraded from 3.8.0 must remove `auth.oidc.apiGateway` and `auth.authorization`, which the 4.0.0 chart rejects. See 3.8.0 to 4.0.0."},"603":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-130","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#install-and-verify-administrative-access","content":"Sign in with an identity holding `pki-admin`. Confirm it can access authorization administration and perform a non-destructive read operation."},"604":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-131","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#test-an-unprivileged-identity","content":"Use a second user without the role and confirm the same operation is denied. This test catches misread claims, overly broad policies and accidental `failOpen` configurations."},"605":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-132","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#reduce-use-of-the-bootstrap-administrator","content":"Create operational principals with narrower policies. Reserve `pki-admin` for authorization administration and recovery, not for daily work."},"606":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-133","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#fastlane-bootstrap","content":"Fastlane installs a Keycloak realm for the lab and creates the user `lamassu` with the temporary password `lamassu`, the role `pki-admin` and a mandatory password change. Its bootstrap principal matches through `preferred_username=lamassu`."},"607":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-134","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#fastlane-bootstrap","content":"Change the password on first login. Do not reuse the Fastlane user, password or IdP as a production design."},"608":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-135","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#design-least-privilege-roles","content":"Avoid reproducing your company's internal structure with dozens of nearly identical policies. Start from the responsibilities that actually need access:"},"609":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-136","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#design-least-privilege-roles","content":"**Authorization administration**: manages principals, policies and grants. It should belong to a small, separate group."},"610":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-137","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#design-least-privilege-roles","content":"**PKI operation**: administers CAs, profiles and certificates, but not necessarily who gets access."},"611":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-138","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#design-least-privilege-roles","content":"**Device registration**: operates devices and DMSs without receiving permissions over keys or authorization configuration."},"612":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-139","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#design-least-privilege-roles","content":"**Audit**: reviews configuration and activity without creating, modifying, signing, revoking or deleting."},"613":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-140","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#design-least-privilege-roles","content":"**Automation**: uses a technical account or a separate certificate, with permissions limited to the flow and resources it controls."},"614":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-141","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#design-least-privilege-roles","content":"For each role, separate \"view\" from \"change\", limit resources through grants, relations or attributes and avoid `*` unless the role must automatically cover future actions."},"615":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-142","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#design-least-privilege-roles","content":"A rule with `actions: [\"*\"]` expands to every action defined by the schema. When a new version adds an action, a wildcard policy may start granting it. Review these policies on every upgrade."},"616":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-143","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#changes-and-access-revocation","content":"To revoke access immediately, disable the principal or revoke its grants. Disabling a principal keeps its configuration and associations for investigation or restoration, but it stops taking part in matching."},"617":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-144","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#changes-and-access-revocation","content":"Deleting a role or group in the IdP prevents new tokens from containing the claim, but an already-issued token may remain valid until it expires. If removal is urgent, combine the IdP change with disabling the principal in Lamassu and revoking sessions or tokens at the provider."},"618":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-145","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#changes-and-access-revocation","content":"When you edit a shared policy, remember the change affects all its principals. To test a new scope, create a separate policy, grant it to a test identity and validate allowed and denied operations before replacing the old one."},"619":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-146","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#operational-checklist","content":"Keep `failOpen: false` unless a documented risk assessment justifies otherwise."},"620":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-147","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#operational-checklist","content":"Use groups or stable roles for people and independent identities for automations."},"621":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-148","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#operational-checklist","content":"Keep at least two recovery administrators and test their access periodically."},"622":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-149","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#operational-checklist","content":"Review active principals, their matches and their grants after IdP changes."},"623":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-150","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#operational-checklist","content":"Search for wildcards in policies before upgrading Lamassu."},"624":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-151","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#operational-checklist","content":"Review `skip_authz` routes and `default_action` settings in HTTP schemas when integrating or upgrading a service."},"625":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-152","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#operational-checklist","content":"Always test one allowed and one denied operation for each role."},"626":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-153","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#operational-checklist","content":"Correlate changes to principals, policies and grants with the audit logs."},"627":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-154","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#the-response-is-401","content":"Authentication failed before permissions were evaluated. Check the JWT signature and expiration, issuer, audience and the availability of the JWKS configured in the Gateway. For X.509, check that the client certificate reaches the point that extracts the credential."},"628":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-155","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#the-response-is-403","content":"The credential could be processed but did not produce a positive authorization. Review in this order:"},"629":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-156","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#the-response-is-403","content":"that an active principal of the correct type exists;"},"630":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-157","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#the-response-is-403","content":"that the claim paths and values match the real token exactly;"},"631":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-158","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#the-response-is-403","content":"that all of the principal's conditions hold;"},"632":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-159","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#the-response-is-403","content":"that the principal has the expected policy granted;"},"633":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-160","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#the-response-is-403","content":"that the policy includes the action and the requested resource type or route;"},"634":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-161","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#the-response-is-403","content":"that the identifier, relation, column filter or HTTP constraint includes the real resource."},"635":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-162","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#the-response-is-403","content":"In the `authz` logs, an external endpoint decision includes `allowed`, `reason`, `matched_principals`, `evaluated_policy_ids`, `matched_policy_id` and the status code. These fields let you separate a matching failure from a permissions failure. With OpenTelemetry tracing enabled, a request that reaches the policy engine produces an `engine.CheckHTTPRequest` span whose attributes record `authz.allowed`, the matched policy and the matched principal. Correlation with the Gateway trace requires trace context to be propagated to authz."},"636":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-163","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#everything-returns-403","content":"Check that the bootstrap principal was created and that the policies were preloaded by the migration Job. Also verify that `services.authz.jwkUrl` is reachable from the `authz` pod; do not assume that a URL accessible from the browser also works inside the cluster."},"637":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-164","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#access-appears-without-a-policy-grant","content":"The path may be covered by a schema-level decision rather than by a policy: routes marked `skip_authz` allow any identity that matches an active principal, and a request under a `base_paths` prefix whose schema sets `default_action: allow` is likewise allowed without consulting policies. Confirm which of the two applies before looking for missing or misassigned grants."},"638":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-165","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#everything-fails-when-authz-is-unavailable","content":"This is the expected behavior with `failOpen: false`. Restore the service, its PostgreSQL connection and its JWKS connectivity. Do not temporarily switch to `failOpen: true` without accepting that protected routes could become accessible without an authorization decision."},"639":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control-166","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/access-control#everything-fails-when-authz-is-unavailable","content":"Continue with Audit logs to investigate configuration changes or with Troubleshooting to diagnose the deployment."},"640":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"page","content":"Alerts and subscriptions","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Administration"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts"},"641":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","content":"Send PKI events to people and external systems."},"642":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"643":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#available-channels","content":"Available channels"},"644":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#create-a-subscription","content":"Create a subscription"},"645":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#choose-the-event","content":"Choose the event"},"646":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#configure-the-destination","content":"Configure the destination"},"647":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#limit-the-notifications","content":"Limit the notifications"},"648":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#review-and-activate","content":"Review and activate"},"649":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#configure-the-webhook-http-client","content":"Configure the webhook HTTP client"},"650":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#webhook-delivery-rules","content":"Webhook delivery rules"},"651":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#manage-a-subscription","content":"Manage a subscription"},"652":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#event-families","content":"Event families"},"653":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","content":"Subscriptions turn Lamassu events into actionable notifications. You can alert a team, feed an incident system or trigger an automation when a CA, certificate or device changes."},"654":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#how-it-works","content":"A service publishes a domain event."},"655":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#how-it-works","content":"Lamassu evaluates the subscriptions associated with that event type."},"656":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#how-it-works","content":"Each subscription's filter decides whether it should be notified."},"657":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#how-it-works","content":"Lamassu delivers the event to the configured channel."},"658":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#how-it-works","content":"The event inventory shows when each type was last observed, how many times it has occurred and how many subscriptions it has. You can expand an event to inspect an example of its JSON payload before creating the filter."},"659":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#available-channels","content":"**Email** sends alerts to a person or an operational list. It only requires the destination address. Event content is rendered as HTML-escaped text, never as markup."},"660":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#available-channels","content":"**Microsoft Teams** posts the notification to a channel through its webhook URL."},"661":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#available-channels","content":"**Webhook** delivers the event to an automation, SIEM or incident system via `POST` or `PUT`."},"662":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#available-channels","content":"The Microsoft Teams and Webhook channels accept an optional `http_client` block that authenticates the call to the receiver. `auth_mode` selects `noauth` (the default), `apikey`, `jwt` or `mtls`; each mode requires its own options:"},"663":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#available-channels","content":"`apikey_options` requires `header` and `key`."},"664":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#available-channels","content":"`jwt_options` requires `oidc_client_id`, `oidc_client_secret` and an absolute `http` or `https` `oidc_well_known`."},"665":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#available-channels","content":"`mtls_options` requires `cert_content` and `key_content` as Base64-encoded PEM, like certificates elsewhere in the API; plain PEM is also accepted. Values that reference files on the server are rejected, and the pair must decode to a matching certificate and private key."},"666":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#available-channels","content":"The alerts API reference documents the full `http_client` schema."},"667":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#choose-the-event","content":"Open **Alerts**, locate the event type and select **Subscribe**. Review the latest JSON example to identify the fields you will need to filter on."},"668":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#configure-the-destination","content":"Select Email, Microsoft Teams or Webhook and enter the channel details."},"669":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#limit-the-notifications","content":"Add a filter if you don't want to receive every instance of the event."},"670":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#limit-the-notifications","content":"**None** notifies all instances of the event."},"671":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#limit-the-notifications","content":"**JSON Path** evaluates one or more specific fields."},"672":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#limit-the-notifications","content":"**JSON Schema** accepts only payloads with a particular structure."},"673":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#limit-the-notifications","content":"**JavaScript** lets you express custom logic. Each filter runs for at most 100 milliseconds; a filter that exceeds this limit fails the condition and the notification is skipped with the error `javascript filter execution timed out`."},"674":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#limit-the-notifications","content":"For example, `function (event) { return event.data.status == \"NO_IDENTITY\"; }` limits a subscription to devices without an identity."},"675":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#limit-the-notifications","content":"The console evaluates the filter against the JSON shown in the **Input Event** editor, which is prefilled with the latest event, and reports whether it matches. For JSON Path and JavaScript filters, it shows **The filter matches this Cloud Event** or **The filter does not match this Cloud Event**. JSON Path expressions are evaluated against the full Cloud Event, so the default `$.data` selects the event's `data` field, and the expression must start with `$`."},"676":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#review-and-activate","content":"Check the event, channel and filter in the summary. Select **Confirm Subscription** to start delivery."},"677":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#configure-the-webhook-http-client","content":"The Webhook and Microsoft Teams channels show this configuration in the subscribe form, at the channel step, and again when editing a subscription; Email does not use it. The fields map to the optional `http_client` block described above:"},"678":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#configure-the-webhook-http-client","content":"**Log Level** selects `debug`, `info`, `warn` or `error`; `info` is the default."},"679":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#configure-the-webhook-http-client","content":"**Call Timeout** defaults to 10 seconds. The console rejects a value above 30 seconds with `Webhook timeout must be at most 30s.`; the API clamps the same value to the cap instead (see Calls are bounded)."},"680":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#configure-the-webhook-http-client","content":"There is no TLS-verification switch for these channels, because the service always verifies the receiver certificate (see TLS is always verified)."},"681":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#configure-the-webhook-http-client","content":"**HTTP Authentication** selects `No Authentication` (the default), `API Key` (API key value and Header Name, `X-API-Key` by default), `OIDC Client Credentials` (Client ID, Client Secret and Well-Known URL) or `Mutual TLS` (Client Certificate and Client Private Key pasted as PEM). A stored private key stays hidden until you select **Show**."},"682":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#configure-the-webhook-http-client","content":"A `http://` URL shows the console warning `Unencrypted HTTP connection` (see the Credentials over http\\:// callout below)."},"683":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#configure-the-webhook-http-client","content":"The form validates inline against the same delivery rules: the webhook URL and the OIDC Well-Known URL must be absolute `http` or `https` URLs, an API-key header may not use a reserved name, and the mTLS certificate and key must be PEM content, not file paths."},"684":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#configure-the-webhook-http-client","content":"The summary in the Confirm step shows the authentication as `None`, `OIDC client credentials`, `API key` or `Mutual TLS`. The subscription details show the authentication, the API key header name (never the value), the OIDC issuer URL, mTLS as `Configured` and a fixed `TLS verification: Verified` row. The API key, client secret and private key are not shown in the subscription details."},"685":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#webhook-delivery-rules","content":"Notifications delivered through the Microsoft Teams and Webhook channels follow a fixed HTTP policy:"},"686":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#webhook-delivery-rules","content":"**TLS is always verified.** The receiver certificate is checked against the system trust store. `insecure_skip_verify` is enforced as `false` — including when it is set to `true` — so self-signed or otherwise untrusted receivers fail delivery."},"687":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#webhook-delivery-rules","content":"**Redirects are not followed.** A `3xx` response fails with `unexpected status code: <n>: redirects are not followed`. Configure `webhook_url` with the final absolute `http` or `https` URL: an `http://` address that an ingress redirects to `https://` stops working."},"688":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#webhook-delivery-rules","content":"**Calls are bounded.** A call defaults to a 10 second timeout; a configured `call_timeout` is capped at 30 seconds. Values above the cap are clamped, not rejected."},"689":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#webhook-delivery-rules","content":"**The response body is ignored.** Delivery checks the status code only, so the receiver may answer with any body."},"690":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#webhook-delivery-rules","content":"**API-key headers are restricted.** A custom `apikey_options.header` may not use names that the platform or receiving services trust — for example `X-Principal-Id`, `X-Request-Id`, `Host`, `Content-Type` or `Forwarded` — and no name may start with `X-Forwarded-`, `X-Envoy-` or `X-Lms-`. Comparisons are case-insensitive."},"691":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#webhook-delivery-rules","content":"**Invalid configurations are rejected at subscribe time.** A channel configuration that would fail on every delivery returns HTTP 400 with a body that starts with `struct validation error:`, and the subscription is not created."},"692":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#webhook-delivery-rules","content":"Credentials are sent regardless of the URL scheme. With an `http://` `webhook_url`, the API key or bearer token travels in cleartext and mTLS has no effect. Prefer `https://` for `webhook_url`, `oidc_well_known` and the token endpoint it advertises."},"693":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#manage-a-subscription","content":"Open an existing subscription to review its destination and filter, modify the configuration or select **Unsubscribe**. Remove subscriptions that no longer have an operational owner to avoid ignored deliveries or stale endpoints."},"694":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#manage-a-subscription","content":"Subscriptions created with older console versions may store the webhook target under `url` and `method` instead of `webhook_url` and `webhook_method`. The service delivers only through `webhook_url` and `webhook_method`, so such a subscription does not deliver even though the subscription details show the stored target. Open the subscription and save it again: the edit form prefills the stored target, and saving rewrites the channel configuration in the current layout."},"695":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#event-families","content":"**Authorities:** `ca.create`, `ca.import`, `ca.reissue` and `ca.delete`."},"696":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#event-families","content":"**Certificates:** `ca.sign.certificate` and `certificate.delete`."},"697":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#event-families","content":"**Profiles:** `profile.issuance.create`, `profile.issuance.update` and `profile.issuance.delete`."},"698":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#event-families","content":"**Enrollment:** `dms.create`, `dms.update`, `dms.enroll` and `dms.reenroll`."},"699":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#event-families","content":"**Devices:** `device.create`, `device.identity.update` and `device.status.update`."},"700":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#event-families","content":"**Validation:** `va.role.crl.create`, `va.crl-settings.init` and `va.crl-settings.update`."},"701":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#event-families","content":"**Keys:** `kms.create`, `kms.import`, `kms.sign` and `kms.delete`."},"702":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#event-families","content":"Use the catalog shown in the console as the source for the types available in your deployed version."},"703":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/alerts#event-families","content":"Since 4.0.0, `va.crl-settings.init` and `va.crl-settings.update` carry the CRL settings of a CA (`ca_id`) and replace `va.role.crl.init` and `va.role.update`. The upgrade migration renames the types of existing subscriptions automatically, but it does not rewrite their conditions: review filters that read the old payload or the old `crl/<ski>` subject, including filters for `va.role.crl.create` (see 3.8.0 to 4.0.0)."},"704":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"page","content":"Audit logs","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Administration"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs"},"705":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","content":"Understand which audit events Lamassu generates and how to turn them into a durable trail."},"706":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#what-an-event-contains","content":"What an event contains"},"707":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#coverage","content":"Coverage"},"708":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#publication-and-persistence","content":"Publication and persistence"},"709":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#sensitive-data","content":"Sensitive data"},"710":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#a-reproducible-investigation","content":"A reproducible investigation"},"711":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#bound-the-interval","content":"Bound the interval"},"712":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#identify-the-operation","content":"Identify the operation"},"713":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#attribute-the-principal","content":"Attribute the principal"},"714":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#compare-intent-and-result","content":"Compare intent and result"},"715":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#follow-the-effect","content":"Follow the effect"},"716":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#periodic-verification","content":"Periodic verification"},"717":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","content":"Lamassu instruments the mutable operations of its services with audit events. Each event describes the operation, the principals that matched, the input, the result and whether it ended in error."},"718":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#what-an-event-contains","content":"The audit body includes:"},"719":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#what-an-event-contains","content":"input: data received by the operation;"},"720":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#what-an-event-contains","content":"has\\_error: whether the service returned an error;"},"721":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#what-an-event-contains","content":"output: produced result or error message;"},"722":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#what-an-event-contains","content":"principals: identifiers of the principals that matched the request."},"723":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#what-an-event-contains","content":"Successful operations use a type prefixed with audit.. Failures publish the operation type suffixed with .error. The CloudEvents event additionally adds source, identifier, date and type."},"724":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#what-an-event-contains","content":"The middlewares publish the record after executing the operation, whether it succeeded or returned an error. This lets you investigate attempts as well as confirmed changes."},"725":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#coverage","content":"The backend applies auditing to mutations of:"},"726":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#coverage","content":"authorities, certificates and issuance profiles;"},"727":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#coverage","content":"keys and KMS engines;"},"728":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#coverage","content":"devices and identities;"},"729":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#coverage","content":"DMSs and enrollment operations;"},"730":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#coverage","content":"validation functions and CRL;"},"731":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#coverage","content":"principals, policies and authorization grants."},"732":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#coverage","content":"Do not confuse these events with domain events. A domain event announces that a resource changed so another component can react; the audit event keeps input, output and principal context for investigation."},"733":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#publication-and-persistence","content":"Services publish audit records to the event bus when their PublisherEventBus is enabled. The backend code does not, by itself, implement a queryable, durable audit file."},"734":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#publication-and-persistence","content":"If you need retention, search, tamper protection or regulatory export, connect a consumer that persists the events into the system approved by your organization."},"735":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#publication-and-persistence","content":"Design the consumer to:"},"736":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#publication-and-persistence","content":"subscribe to the audit.# types and also to operation types ending in .error;"},"737":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#publication-and-persistence","content":"keep the complete CloudEvent unmodified;"},"738":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#publication-and-persistence","content":"record the ingestion time and detect duplicates by ID;"},"739":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#publication-and-persistence","content":"encrypt in transit and at rest;"},"740":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#publication-and-persistence","content":"restrict reading and deletion to a role separate from the PKI operator;"},"741":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#publication-and-persistence","content":"apply an explicit retention and legal hold policy;"},"742":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#publication-and-persistence","content":"alert if it stops consuming or the pending queue grows."},"743":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#sensitive-data","content":"The input and output fields can contain subjects, metadata, public material, configuration or error messages. Evaluate their classification before sending them to an external platform."},"744":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#sensitive-data","content":"Do not log private keys, provider secrets or full tokens in automations around Lamassu. Restrict export and apply redaction at the destination without destroying the fields needed for attribution."},"745":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#bound-the-interval","content":"Start from the reported time and normalize every source to UTC."},"746":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#identify-the-operation","content":"Filter by event type, service source and resource identifier."},"747":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#attribute-the-principal","content":"Review principals and correlate them with the OIDC provider or the X.509 identity valid at that moment."},"748":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#compare-intent-and-result","content":"Contrast input, has\\_error and output. A failed attempt does not mean the resource changed."},"749":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#follow-the-effect","content":"Look for the domain events and service records that share resource and time window. In a CA revocation, include the cascading operations."},"750":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#periodic-verification","content":"Generate a controlled mutation in a test environment and check that:"},"751":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#periodic-verification","content":"a successful audit event appears;"},"752":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#periodic-verification","content":"the principal matches the identity used;"},"753":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#periodic-verification","content":"the consumer persists it exactly once;"},"754":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#periodic-verification","content":"it can be retrieved by resource, actor and period;"},"755":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#periodic-verification","content":"a consumer outage raises an alert."},"756":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/administration/audit-logs#periodic-verification","content":"For metrics, traces and technical logs of the deployment, see Troubleshooting. Audit answers \"who tried to change what\"; observability explains how the system behaved."},"757":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","type":"page","content":"Platform architecture","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture"},"758":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","content":"Lamassu components and how control, keys, issuance and devices relate."},"759":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture#control-plane","content":"Control plane"},"760":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture#key-custody-and-cryptographic-operations","content":"Key custody and cryptographic operations"},"761":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture#issuance-and-enrollment","content":"Issuance and enrollment"},"762":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture#status-and-validation","content":"Status and validation"},"763":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture#platform-dependencies","content":"Platform dependencies"},"764":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","content":"Lamassu deploys as a set of independent services. This separation keeps every component from needing direct access to private keys and lets each capability scale according to load."},"765":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","content":"Switch to the low level to see the internals of the Lamassu platform box (CA, KMS, DMS, Device Manager, VA, Alerts, AWS IoT connector, Job Manager and the console/API), and to medium to see it as a single platform alongside its external dependencies."},"766":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture#control-plane","content":"The console and the APIs manage authorities, certificates, DMSs, devices, alerts and configuration. Domain events allow connectors and automations to react to changes without continuously polling the platform."},"767":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture#key-custody-and-cryptographic-operations","content":"The KMS offers a common interface over software engines, PKCS#11 and cloud providers. The selected engine keeps the key or delegates the cryptographic operation without the other services knowing its implementation."},"768":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture#issuance-and-enrollment","content":"The CA service issues certificates and maintains the relationship with its authority. The DMS applies the enrollment rules and exposes the EST flows so a device can request or renew an identity."},"769":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture#status-and-validation","content":"Device Manager keeps the operational view of the device and its history. The Validation Authority publishes OCSP and CRLs so other systems can decide whether to trust a presented certificate."},"770":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/architecture#platform-dependencies","content":"In a self-managed deployment, Lamassu uses PostgreSQL for persistence, RabbitMQ for messaging and an OIDC provider for authentication. See the deployment architecture for how the services are published on Kubernetes."},"771":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","type":"page","content":"How Lamassu works","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview"},"772":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","content":"The mental model of trust, keys, certificates and devices."},"773":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"The model in five pieces"},"774":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"From onboarding to operation"},"775":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","content":"Lamassu connects three elements: a **root of trust**, an **issuance policy** and an **entity that needs to prove its identity**. The platform coordinates these elements throughout the certificate lifecycle."},"776":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"**Cryptographic engine.** Generates or safeguards keys and executes private-key operations without exposing key material to the rest of the services."},"777":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"**Certification Authority (CA).** Signs certificates and establishes the chain of trust."},"778":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"**Device Management Service (DMS).** Defines how the devices of a fleet are registered, authenticated and renewed."},"779":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"**Device.** Keeps its private key and presents the certificate to prove its identity."},"780":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"**Validation Authority (VA).** Publishes the status of certificates through OCSP and CRL."},"781":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"An administrator configures a cryptographic engine and creates or imports a CA."},"782":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"A DMS relates that CA to an enrollment policy."},"783":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"The device generates a key and requests a certificate through EST, or an operator assigns it an identity."},"784":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"Lamassu keeps the inventory, history and status of the identity."},"785":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"Consumers check the chain and query OCSP or a CRL when they need to know whether it is still valid."},"786":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"<Card title=\"Architecture\" description=\"Get to know the components and where each one's responsibility ends.\" href=\"/docs/platform/concepts/architecture\" />"},"787":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"<Card title=\"Identity lifecycle\" description=\"Follow a certificate from enrollment to renewal or revocation.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle\" />"},"788":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"page","content":"Devices and identities","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","IoT Fleets","Devices and identities"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management"},"789":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","content":"Register, inspect and retire devices while checking their current identity and history."},"790":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"Device states"},"791":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#inspect-a-device","content":"Inspect a device"},"792":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#register-a-device-manually","content":"Register a device manually"},"793":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#create-the-device","content":"Create the device"},"794":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#define-its-membership","content":"Define its membership"},"795":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#classify-the-device","content":"Classify the device"},"796":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#verify-the-registration","content":"Verify the registration"},"797":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#assign-an-identity-manually","content":"Assign an identity manually"},"798":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#revoke-the-current-identity","content":"Revoke the current identity"},"799":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#decommission-a-device","content":"Decommission a device"},"800":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#automate-enrollment","content":"Automate enrollment"},"801":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","content":"This guide is for a fleet operator. You need device, DMS and certificate permissions for the intended actions. A fleet is organized through these resources, tags and metadata; there is no separate “fleet” object to create."},"802":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","content":"Each device has a `Device ID`, one owning DMS (`dms_owner`) and, once provisioned, an identity slot with an active version and previous versions. In these flows, keep the CSR and certificate `Common Name` equal to `Device ID`: binding uses that CN to update the device."},"803":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"Operational view"},"804":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"Meaning"},"805":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"**No Identity**"},"806":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"A record exists without an associated identity."},"807":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"**Active**"},"808":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"The slot is active; also check certificate dates, status and usages."},"809":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"**Renewal Pending**"},"810":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"The identity is in the operational renewal window."},"811":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"**Expiring Soon**"},"812":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"Expiration is approaching according to configured thresholds."},"813":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"**Expired**"},"814":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"The identity has expired."},"815":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"**Revoked**"},"816":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"The identity is marked revoked."},"817":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"**Decommissioned**"},"818":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"The record is retired and ordinary updates do not restore operation."},"819":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#device-states","content":"Device, slot and certificate states are distinct. Events and jobs can update the view after saving a certificate; an **Active** label does not establish consumer acceptance."},"820":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#inspect-a-device","content":"Filter the inventory by ID, tags and status. Open details and record the owning DMS, active version and current certificate serial."},"821":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#inspect-a-device","content":"**Certificate History** relates previous and current versions. Replacing the slot does not by itself revoke every previous version."},"822":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#inspect-a-device","content":"**Device Event Timeline** helps reconstruct registration, provisioning, renewal and status changes. A change may be saved even if event persistence fails; also inspect the record and certificates."},"823":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#inspect-a-device","content":"Compare these values with the identity installed on the device. Updating a Lamassu slot does not install files on the remote equipment."},"824":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#register-a-device-manually","content":"Use this flow to prepare inventory or assign an identity through the console. You need an existing DMS."},"825":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#create-the-device","content":"Open registration in **Managed Devices**. Confirm the ID does not already exist in another DMS: ID lookup is not restricted to a fleet."},"826":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#define-its-membership","content":"Enter **Device ID** and select its owning DMS. The console’s **Registration Authority** label refers to that DMS."},"827":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#classify-the-device","content":"Add model, environment or location tags and an icon according to your inventory."},"828":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#verify-the-registration","content":"Read the device again: require the intended DMS and **No Identity**. Follow Manual registration to complete assignment."},"829":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#verify-the-registration","content":"Preregistration does not establish that `/simpleenroll` will admit the request. Review its interaction with `enable_replaceable_enrollment` in Provisioning strategies."},"830":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#assign-an-identity-manually","content":"From **No Identity**, use **Assign Identity**:"},"831":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#assign-an-identity-manually","content":"Select an active, current certificate suitable for the consumer, with `CN` exactly equal to `Device ID`."},"832":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#assign-an-identity-manually","content":"If unavailable, **Issue New Instead** starts issuance using the intended CA. Review the profile first."},"833":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#assign-an-identity-manually","content":"Confirm and read the serial, active version and history again."},"834":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#assign-an-identity-manually","content":"Install the key/certificate pair and required intermediates on the device and test usage."},"835":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#assign-an-identity-manually","content":"Issuing, binding and installing are separate steps. If an operation fails, check which steps persisted before repeating it."},"836":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#revoke-the-current-identity","content":"Locate the active serial in history and revoke it with an appropriate reason. Verify the record, OCSP/CRL publication and rejection of a new consumer connection using the certificate guide."},"837":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#revoke-the-current-identity","content":"Revocation does not remove the device. It does not automatically enable another enrollment either: recovery depends on its credential, status and DMS policy. `CertificateHold` can be reactivated under PKI conditions; other reasons block subsequent certificate changes."},"838":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#decommission-a-device","content":"Before **Decommission**, inventory active and previous identities, connections and destination permissions. Prepare retirement in the consumer."},"839":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#decommission-a-device","content":"The backend saves **Decommissioned** and attempts to revoke the active version’s certificate with `CessationOfOperation` if the slot was not expired or revoked. It does not traverse all history. Deferred revocation can fail after retirement is saved; check the result by serial."},"840":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#decommission-a-device","content":"Retired status protects ordinary device and slot updates. It does not guarantee that every EST request is rejected before issuance: binding can skip a retired device without returning an error. Check for remaining usable certificates or permissions and block new admission in the relevant control."},"841":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#decommission-a-device","content":"Retain records according to audit policy. Do not reuse a retired ID to hide an equipment change."},"842":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#automate-enrollment","content":"<Card title=\"Enroll and connect a device\" description=\"Obtain an identity from the client and test mTLS.\" href=\"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device\" />"},"843":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/device-management#automate-enrollment","content":"<Card title=\"Renewal and recovery\" description=\"Install the successor and handle failures without losing known state.\" href=\"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/renewal-and-recovery\" />"},"844":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","type":"page","content":"Bootstrap identity and authentication","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","IoT Fleets","Devices and identities","Enrollment with PKI"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity"},"845":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","content":"Prepare server trust and admission proofs for enroll and reenroll."},"846":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#initial-server-trust","content":"Initial server trust"},"847":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#bootstrap-credential","content":"Bootstrap credential"},"848":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#modes-per-operation","content":"Modes per operation"},"849":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#webhook-contract","content":"Webhook contract"},"850":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#revocation-and-checks","content":"Revocation and checks"},"851":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","content":"This guide connects the DMS administrator with device manufacturing and integration. Before requesting an operational identity, the client must authenticate the EST server and establish entitlement to request the intended ID."},"852":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#initial-server-trust","content":"Install a previously verified root, chain or pin through a trusted channel: manufacturing, approved configuration or authenticated distribution. It enables TLS and server-name verification before downloading `/cacerts`."},"853":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#initial-server-trust","content":"Your only trust proof cannot come from the same unauthenticated server. The EST server TLS certificate, bootstrap certificate and operational identity issuer may belong to different hierarchies."},"854":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#bootstrap-credential","content":"With `CLIENT_CERTIFICATE`, the device presents its initial certificate and proves key possession through TLS. The DMS validates it against admission CAs. In the inspected flow, the validator receives one leaf credential: configure and test the direct issuer for the simple case; sending more intermediates does not establish delivery to the service."},"855":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#bootstrap-credential","content":"Check dates, matching certificate/key and revocation before provisioning. A credential shared across equipment identifies that shared credential, not an individual device."},"856":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#bootstrap-credential","content":"Initial mTLS validation does not by itself compare bootstrap CN with the requested CSR CN. If a requester should only request its own `Device ID`, add a control binding credential to ID, such as the combined webhook, and test a request with another CN. Certificate re-enrollment does compare its CN to the CSR; subsequent checks use the registered active identity."},"857":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#modes-per-operation","content":"Select the four modes independently for enrollment and re-enrollment in DMS. Renewal credentials depend on that block; do not assume the bootstrap is always used or the webhook disappears."},"858":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#modes-per-operation","content":"An administrative OIDC token is not a native EST mode. A webhook may interpret an agreed credential header; that service then performs authorization. In NO\\_AUTH, sending a token does not add DMS authentication."},"859":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#webhook-contract","content":"The DMS sends operation context to the configured service. Method comes from configuration; agree the contract before selecting POST or PUT. Authorization wait defaults to 10 seconds, replaced by a configured positive timeout. The DMS verifies the receiver certificate unless `insecure_skip_verify` is enabled in the webhook config — verification is on by default — and does not follow redirects, so the configured URL must be the final one. The authorization response must be JSON of at most 1 MiB. With Lamassu-to-webhook authentication configured over `http://`, the API key or bearer token travels in cleartext, and mTLS has no effect because no TLS handshake takes place, so the client certificate is never presented; prefer `https://`. Configure those options in the webhook settings of the DMS guide."},"860":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#webhook-contract","content":"Example body:"},"861":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#webhook-contract","content":"`csr` is **base64 of PEM**, unlike the EST body, which is base64 of DER. `http_request` contains URL and first header entries from available HTTP context. This body does not include an `operation` field; distinguish enroll and reenroll through the path and configured policy."},"862":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#webhook-contract","content":"The webhook should verify credential, its relationship to `device_cn`, DMS, operation and admission policy. Forwarded headers are not themselves trusted evidence. **Lamassu-to-webhook authentication** is a separate relationship configured in the server’s HTTP client."},"863":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#webhook-contract","content":"Continuation requires a successful HTTP response and JSON:"},"864":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#webhook-contract","content":"A bodyless `204` does not satisfy the contract. Denial, transport error, uninterpretable response or timeout abort authorization. Combined mode validates the certificate first, then queries the webhook. See the webhook specification."},"865":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#revocation-and-checks","content":"The DMS first looks up the certificate in Lamassu; for external certificates it attempts OCSP and CRL. If revocation cannot be checked, validators can continue treating it as not revoked. The code also does not establish rejection of every external status other than Good. Test required behavior with your actual credential and endpoint; do not present this as guaranteed strict enforcement across every source."},"866":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity#revocation-and-checks","content":"Test an allowed certificate, an incorrect one, another CN, webhook denial, timeout and re-enrollment under its own policy. Keep results and schedule bootstrap credential retirement where appropriate. Continue with EST client."},"867":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms","type":"page","content":"Configure and operate the DMS","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","IoT Fleets","Devices and identities","Enrollment with PKI"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms"},"868":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms","content":"Define registration, authentication per operation, issuance, renewal and distributed trust."},"869":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"870":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms#configure-a-dms","content":"Configure a DMS"},"871":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms#identify-the-fleet","content":"Identify the fleet"},"87