cture-at-a-glance","content":"The provisioning administrator configures the DMS and initial trust."},"1741":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"The device client requests a certificate and installs it with the matching key."},"1742":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"The consumer validates the identity and applies its access permissions."},"1743":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"See How Lamassu works to understand the resources and platform architecture for the services. Installation, network exposure and dependencies are explained in Deployment."},"1744":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#build-your-trust-hierarchy","content":"Create or incorporate authorities and organize their relationships in PKI. The hierarchy and its rotation determine which chains consumers must recognize."},"1745":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#protect-cryptographic-keys","content":"Choose the engine that keeps authority keys and control who can use them. See Keys and engines; provider setup belongs to deployment."},"1746":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#issue-and-control-certificates","content":"Define issuance profiles, sign requests and review the certificate inventory. Check the issued certificate from the client that will use it."},"1747":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#automate-device-identities","content":"Configure a DMS and use EST to request and renew certificates. Preparing the initial credential and installing the result belong to device integration."},"1748":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#publish-validation-status","content":"Use OCSP and CRL to publish revocation status. Each consumer must configure how it retrieves and applies that information."},"1749":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#react-to-events","content":"Use audit logs to investigate changes and configure alerts and subscriptions to react to lifecycle events."},"1750":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"Responsibility"},"1751":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"What it prepares or checks"},"1752":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"PKI administrator"},"1753":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"Key custody, CA hierarchy, profiles and validation."},"1754":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"Fleet administrator"},"1755":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"DMS, device admission, renewal policy and inventory."},"1756":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"Device integrator"},"1757":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"Initial credential, server trust, EST client, and key and certificate storage."},"1758":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"Consumer integrator"},"1759":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"Issuer trust, certificate validation and permissions in the destination."},"1760":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"Infrastructure operator"},"1761":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"Installation, network, availability, dependencies and deployment diagnosis."},"1762":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/overview#operational-reference","content":"The API reference contains contracts for automating operations. To investigate a failure, start in the affected section: PKI, EST or Deployment."},"1763":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"page","content":"CA hierarchy and rotation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Keys, authorities and certificates"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation"},"1764":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","content":"Design root and intermediate authorities and replace certificates or keys without breaking trust."},"1765":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"Design the hierarchy"},"1766":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"Reissuance and rotation are not the same"},"1767":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"When to choose each operation"},"1768":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#key-rotation-procedure","content":"Key rotation procedure"},"1769":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#inventory-the-dependencies","content":"Inventory the dependencies"},"1770":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#create-the-successor-ca","content":"Create the successor CA"},"1771":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#distribute-the-new-trust","content":"Distribute the new trust"},"1772":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#switch-issuance","content":"Switch issuance"},"1773":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#renew-in-batches","content":"Renew in batches"},"1774":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#close-the-overlap","content":"Close the overlap"},"1775":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"Cascading revocation"},"1776":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"Checks after the change"},"1777":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","content":"The hierarchy determines the blast radius of any error or compromise. A root signs intermediate CAs; intermediates issue the identities used by devices and services. This separation lets you isolate environments and rotate a branch without replacing all trust."},"1778":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","content":"This procedure is for the PKI operator replacing an authority in use. You need access to CAs, keys and profiles, a dependency inventory and coordination with trust-store and device owners. Before switching issuance, prepare a test cohort and decide the criterion for ending overlap."},"1779":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"For a production installation, use a very restricted root and one or more operational intermediates. Separate intermediates when any of these boundaries change:"},"1780":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"environment, such as production and preproduction;"},"1781":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"owner or operating team;"},"1782":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"device family or manufacturing process;"},"1783":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"region or regulatory requirement;"},"1784":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"cryptographic engine or key policy;"},"1785":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"maintenance window and renewal cadence."},"1786":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"Avoid deep hierarchies without a concrete need. Each level adds chain distribution, validation and one more certificate you must renew."},"1787":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"A child CA and its end-entity certificates must expire before their issuer. Reserve a margin that allows distributing another chain and renewing dependent certificates."},"1788":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"**Reissuing a CA** creates a new certificate over the existing key. Lamassu generates a CSR with that key, self-signs it if it is a root or asks the parent CA to sign it if it is subordinate. The new certificate becomes active and the CA points to its serial number; the old and new certificates are linked through metadata."},"1789":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"If the CRL settings of the CA are signed by the superseded CA certificate, reissuing moves the signer to the new certificate — provided it carries `cRLSign` — and republishes the CRL. Otherwise, and for settings signed by a different certificate, the signer is kept, so check the new certificate’s key usage after reissuing; see the CRL guide."},"1790":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"**Rotating a CA** creates a successor key and authority. It is the right choice in the face of compromise, a cryptographic change, an engine migration or non-exportable key policies."},"1791":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"Lamassu does not allow reissuing an already-revoked CA or a CA whose expiration date has passed. Plan ahead for both conditions."},"1792":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Reissue if the key is still trustworthy and you only need another validity period or an updated certificate."},"1793":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Rotate the key if compromise is suspected, the algorithm changes or you want to move custody to another engine."},"1794":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Create a parallel branch if you cannot update all consumers at the same time."},"1795":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Revoke immediately only when the risk of keeping the CA outweighs the impact of interrupting the fleet."},"1796":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#inventory-the-dependencies","content":"Locate child CAs, issued certificates, DMSs, connectors and external trust stores. Include devices that may stay offline for weeks or months."},"1797":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#create-the-successor-ca","content":"Generate a new key in the planned engine, create the CA and assign it an explicit profile. Do not reuse the operational identifier to hide that it is a different generation."},"1798":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#distribute-the-new-trust","content":"Add the new root or chain to consumers before issuing with it. If distributing through EST `/cacerts`, explicitly include the required managed CAs and inspect the content; including the issuer does not automatically include every intermediate. Install the new trust in a cohort and verify that it still accepts the previous identity."},"1799":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#switch-issuance","content":"Update the enrollment CA and profile of the DMSs. While old-CA cohorts still renew, add the previous enrollment CA to each DMS's re-enrollment validation CAs (`reenrollment_settings.est_rfc7030_settings.client_certificate_settings.validation_cas`): the new enrollment CA is trusted automatically, but the old one was the enrollment CA and appears in no re-enrollment trust list, so without that entry its certificates can no longer renew. The DMS guide documents the setting."},"1800":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#renew-in-batches","content":"Migrate a small cohort, validate mTLS, OCSP and CRL from the consumer and expand progressively. Monitor which devices still present the old chain."},"1801":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#close-the-overlap","content":"Once no legitimate consumer depends on the previous authority, remove it from issuance, from the re-enrollment validation CAs and from the distributed CAs. Revoke it if policy requires it."},"1802":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"Lamassu saves the CA’s revocation, then attempts to revoke child CAs and issued certificates with `CessationOfOperation`. Propagation continues recursively through child CAs. This is not a transaction over the whole hierarchy: some resources may have changed while other updates failed."},"1803":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"Resources in `EXPIRED` state and resources already revoked for a final reason reject further status transitions. Per-descendant failures are logged; review the inventory and logs even when the parent operation completes."},"1804":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"`CertificateHold` allows reactivating the parent while it is not expired, but does not restore child CAs or certificates permanently revoked during the cascade. Holding a CA therefore does not provide a reversible pause for its entire branch."},"1805":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"Before closing the change, compare the original dependency inventory with final states and verify revocation publication for each issuer. Do not use revocation as the ordinary mechanism to stop issuance: complete migration and remove the CA from operational flows."},"1806":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"The new chain ends in an anchor installed by the consumer."},"1807":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"New certificates contain the expected AKI, SKI, KU, EKU and SAN."},"1808":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"The DMS delivers the correct chain through EST `/cacerts`."},"1809":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"Re-enrollment accepts the old identity during the planned period."},"1810":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"OCSP and CRL respond for the authorities that remain active."},"1811":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"No DMS is left accidentally issuing from the old CA."},"1812":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"See the Trust model to understand the DMS's CA sets and Certificate lifecycle for states and revocation effects."},"1813":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"page","content":"Certification authorities","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Keys, authorities and certificates"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities"},"1814":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","content":"Create, import and operate the authorities that establish your PKI's trust."},"1815":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"Choose a flow"},"1816":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#create-a-new-authority","content":"Create a new authority"},"1817":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"1818":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#open-the-wizard","content":"Open the wizard"},"1819":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-the-key","content":"Configure the key"},"1820":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-the-ca-type","content":"Choose the CA type"},"1821":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"Define the identity"},"1822":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-validity-and-uses","content":"Configure validity and uses"},"1823":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#create-and-verify","content":"Create and verify"},"1824":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#use-a-key-from-the-kms","content":"Use a key from the KMS"},"1825":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#import-an-external-ca","content":"Import an external CA"},"1826":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#select-the-engine","content":"Select the engine"},"1827":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#load-the-material","content":"Load the material"},"1828":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-default-issuance","content":"Define the default issuance"},"1829":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#verify-the-import","content":"Verify the import"},"1830":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Inspect an authority"},"1831":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#issue-certificates","content":"Issue certificates"},"1832":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#revoke-a-ca","content":"Revoke a CA"},"1833":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#assess-the-impact","content":"Assess the impact"},"1834":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#start-the-revocation","content":"Start the revocation"},"1835":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#confirm-the-identity","content":"Confirm the identity"},"1836":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#check-the-publication","content":"Check the publication"},"1837":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#delete-a-ca","content":"Delete a CA"},"1838":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","content":"A certification authority (CA) binds identities to public keys through signed certificates. In Lamassu you can create a new hierarchy, use a key already in the KMS or incorporate an external CA."},"1839":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","content":"To design a full chain or replace an authority in production, see CA hierarchy and rotation. If you need to standardize what each authority can sign, use Certificate profiles."},"1840":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","content":"To administer CAs, you need authority and key permissions, a reachable engine and a reviewed profile. An external consumer does not trust a CA merely because it appears in this inventory: agree root and chain distribution separately."},"1841":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**New CA with a new key:** create a root of trust from scratch. Lamassu generates and keeps the key pair."},"1842":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**New CA from the KMS:** reuse a key already registered in the platform."},"1843":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**Import a CA with its private key:** incorporate an external authority that Lamassu can issue with."},"1844":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**Import only the certificate:** register public material. If Lamassu finds its key in the KMS, it can associate it; otherwise, the CA has no usable key for issuance."},"1845":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"First time here? Follow Create your first CA to complete the minimal journey."},"1846":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"Decide whether the CA will be a root or an intermediate."},"1847":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"Choose the engine that will keep the key."},"1848":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"Define a validity longer than that of the certificates it will issue."},"1849":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"For an intermediate CA, make sure the parent CA is active."},"1850":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#open-the-wizard","content":"In **Certification Authorities**, select **Create New CA** and choose to generate a new key pair."},"1851":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-the-key","content":"Select the cryptographic engine, the algorithm and the size or curve. Lamassu supports RSA and EC keys according to the engine's capabilities."},"1852":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-the-key","content":"Use only sizes and curves supported by the engine and the profile’s cryptographic policy. Read Keys and engines before reusing external material."},"1853":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-the-ca-type","content":"Select **Root CA** for a self-signed authority or **Intermediate CA** for an authority signed by another CA. In the latter case, choose the issuing CA."},"1854":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"Enter a unique **CA Name**. This name becomes the certificate's `Common Name`. Complete the Distinguished Name fields your policy requires:"},"1855":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`C`: two-letter ISO 3166-1 country code."},"1856":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`ST`: state or province."},"1857":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`L`: locality."},"1858":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`O`: organization."},"1859":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`OU`: organizational unit."},"1860":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"The CA's internal identifier is generated automatically and cannot be changed."},"1861":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-validity-and-uses","content":"Define **CA Certificate Expiration** and **Default End-Entity Certificate Issuance Expiration**. You can express a duration (`5y 8w 4d`), pick a date or use the maximum allowed date."},"1862":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-validity-and-uses","content":"Review the CA’s own certificate separately from the default profile for certificates it will issue later. Choose an explicit issuance policy; do not assume the form’s initial values suit your consumers."},"1863":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#create-and-verify","content":"Confirm the form and open the CA. Check status, issuer, dates, associated engine and key. Download the certificate: it should contain `CA:TRUE` and a usage permitting certificate signing. Verify the self-signature for a root or the chain to your root for an intermediate. Complete a test issuance to check that the key can actually sign."},"1864":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#create-and-verify","content":"Plan and verify expiration using the Profiles rules. Issuance does not automatically clamp validity to the issuer’s expiration; leave time to replace the authority and renew identities."},"1865":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#use-a-key-from-the-kms","content":"Select &#x2A;*Create New CA (Existing Key)** when the key is already registered in Lamassu. The wizard first asks for the backing key and then shows the same configuration of type, identity, validity and profile."},"1866":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#use-a-key-from-the-kms","content":"This flow is useful when the key was previously created in an HSM, imported through BYOK or must be reused under a specific custody policy."},"1867":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#import-an-external-ca","content":"You need the CA certificate in PEM, its chain to a known root and, when importing it, an exportable private key. Before uploading material, verify signature, dates, `CA:TRUE`, signing usages (including `cRLSign`, without which the CA cannot publish its CRL) and public-key correspondence. The key verification procedure also compares a CA key and certificate."},"1868":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#import-an-external-ca","content":"The backend rejects an import whose certificate lacks the CA basic constraint (`basicConstraints cA flag is not set`), whose serial number matches a stored certificate with different contents, or whose identical certificate already belongs to an existing CA. A deleted CA's certificate record is kept and can be reused when re-importing the same certificate, including its previous status. Re-importing a different certificate with that serial number is rejected; check the certificate and status after re-importing."},"1869":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#import-an-external-ca","content":"Deleting a CA releases the key references of its own current certificate and linked reissued certificates, while keeping those records for its issuer's CRL and OCSP. It then attempts to delete the key; the KMS keeps it if other certificates still reference it, such as another CA sharing the key. Revoking certificates issued by the deleted CA does not release their own key references."},"1870":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#select-the-engine","content":"Check the installation’s default engine before importing a CA with a key. CA import delegates key import to that engine; it does not guarantee arbitrary provider selection from the form. To select an engine while importing the key separately, use the KMS."},"1871":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#load-the-material","content":"Import the certificate and, when applicable, its PEM key. Register the CAs needed to identify the issuer. Registering a CA does not install it in external trust stores."},"1872":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#load-the-material","content":"The backend validates before importing any key: a duplicate CA ID and a certificate that is not a CA (missing `basicConstraints` `cA=TRUE`) are rejected, the latter with `400` `certificate is not a CA: basicConstraints cA flag is not set`. If a failure occurs after the key was imported, the key is kept in the KMS and a warning tells you to delete it manually."},"1873":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-default-issuance","content":"Associate an explicit issuance profile if the CA will sign. Check usages and dates using Profiles."},"1874":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#verify-the-import","content":"Review the registered type, associated key and engine, and issuer relationship. Certificate-only import may associate an existing KMS key using the certificate’s key identifier. Without a usable key, the CA is public material and cannot sign."},"1875":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#verify-the-import","content":"For an issuing CA, complete a test issuance and check OCSP and CRL. Creating the record alone does not establish key availability, complete chain consistency or status publication."},"1876":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Open a CA from the inventory to review:"},"1877":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Status and validity period."},"1878":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Certificate and chain in PEM format."},"1879":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Number of active, expired and revoked certificates."},"1880":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Certificates issued in **Issued Certificates**."},"1881":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"The CRL linked to the authority."},"1882":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Metadata and the associated cryptographic engine."},"1883":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"You can filter the inventory by name, status and CA type."},"1884":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#issue-certificates","content":"You can start an issuance from **Issued Certificates**, from a CA's action menu or from the global certificate inventory."},"1885":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#issue-certificates","content":"**Generate Key & CSR in Browser** is useful for a manual operation or a quick test. The browser generates the key and you must download it at the end."},"1886":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#issue-certificates","content":"**Upload Existing CSR** is the right option when the key must remain on the target system. Lamassu receives the request but never the private key."},"1887":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#issue-certificates","content":"Follow Issue your first certificate for the guided flow. Certificate management explains the inventory, inspection and revocation."},"1888":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#revoke-a-ca","content":"Revoking a CA prevents issuance and may interrupt its entire branch. Only `CertificateHold` allows reactivating the CA itself if it is not expired. Descendant revocation is attempted with `CessationOfOperation`; reactivating the parent does not restore those descendants. Follow the cascading revocation conditions."},"1889":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#assess-the-impact","content":"Identify the certificates, devices and consumers that depend on the CA. Prepare a replacement authority and chain when necessary."},"1890":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#start-the-revocation","content":"Open the authority and select **Revoke CA**. Choose the reason that describes the incident, for example `KeyCompromise`, `CACompromise`, `Superseded` or `CessationOfOperation`."},"1891":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-77","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#confirm-the-identity","content":"Type the CA's name exactly to enable **Confirm Revocation**."},"1892":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-78","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#check-the-publication","content":"Check **REVOKED** on the CA and review descendants individually; propagation permits partial failures. Independently verify OCSP and CRL publication and consumer rejection. A revoked record does not guarantee that an existing session closes."},"1893":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-79","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#delete-a-ca","content":"Permanent deletion is only available with the CA revoked or expired; a CA imported without a key can be deleted in any state. Delete the record only when your retention and audit policy allows it."},"1894":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-80","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#delete-a-ca","content":"The CA’s CRL settings are kept, and they cannot be removed through the API. The last CRL keeps being served but is never regenerated once the CA is gone, so adjust its validity and signer beforehand (see CRL). The CA’s key is released, but the KMS keeps it while other certificates still reference it."},"1895":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-81","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#delete-a-ca","content":"Lamassu keeps the certificate record of a deleted CA. If that same certificate is imported again, the import succeeds and reuses the record: it updates the type, issuer and key but keeps the status, so the CA reappears in the state it had when deleted (normally revoked or expired). A different certificate with the same serial number is rejected with a 400 error, and a certificate that already belongs to an existing CA with a 409 error. To avoid inheriting the previous status, use a certificate with a different serial number and check the result after importing. The reimported CA is registered under a new, backend-generated CA ID and does not inherit the CRL settings of the deleted CA: those keep serving their last CRL at the CA ID URL, and at `/crl/<ski>` — the URL that certificates issued before the 4.0.0 upgrade carry — when the settings were migrated by that upgrade; when they are archived, they can no longer be edited (see CRL)."},"1896":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"page","content":"Certificate profiles","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Keys, authorities and certificates"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles"},"1897":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","content":"Define reusable policies to issue consistent certificates and constrain accepted keys."},"1898":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#what-a-profile-controls","content":"What a profile controls"},"1899":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#validity","content":"Validity"},"1900":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#ca-certificate-or-end-entity-certificate","content":"CA certificate or end-entity certificate"},"1901":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#key-usage-and-extended-key-usage","content":"Key Usage and Extended Key Usage"},"1902":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#subject","content":"Subject"},"1903":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#csr-extensions","content":"CSR extensions"},"1904":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"Cryptographic constraints"},"1905":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"Profile precedence"},"1906":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#create-a-profile","content":"Create a profile"},"1907":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#define-a-single-purpose","content":"Define a single purpose"},"1908":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#choose-the-validity","content":"Choose the validity"},"1909":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#fix-usages-and-subject","content":"Fix usages and subject"},"1910":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#constrain-the-keys","content":"Constrain the keys"},"1911":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#attach-it-and-test","content":"Attach it and test"},"1912":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#design-examples","content":"Design examples"},"1913":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#changes-and-deletion","content":"Changes and deletion"},"1914":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","content":"An issuance profile turns a certificate policy into reusable configuration. Instead of deciding validity, subject, extensions and algorithms on every request, you define once what is allowed and attach the profile to a CA, a DMS or a specific issuance."},"1915":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","content":"This guide is for the PKI administrator defining issuance policy. You need permissions to manage profiles and associate them with the intended CA or DMS, plus a test consumer with known identity and purpose requirements."},"1916":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#validity","content":"You can express the lifetime as a duration from the moment of issuance or as a fixed end date. A duration works well for recurring identities; a common date is useful to make a whole batch end before a migration or retirement."},"1917":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#validity","content":"Plan the end date within the issuing CA’s validity and leave a renewal margin. The signer calculates the date from the profile; it does not automatically clamp validity to the issuer’s expiration. Check both dates in the resulting certificate. A fixed date in the past does not produce a usable identity either."},"1918":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#ca-certificate-or-end-entity-certificate","content":"`Sign as CA` sets `IsCA` and the basic constraints needed for an authority. Lamassu enforces this: a profile with `Sign as CA` is consumed only when creating or reissuing a CA. Any signing request that resolves to such a profile is rejected — direct signing with a CA, including certificate issuance requests on it, and DMS enrollment or re-enrollment. Nothing validates the profile when it is saved: if a CA's default profile or a DMS profile has `Sign as CA` enabled, the problem appears on the first signing request that resolves to it — for a DMS profile, when a device tries to enroll or re-enroll — and renewal stays blocked until the profile is changed."},"1919":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#key-usage-and-extended-key-usage","content":"The profile can enforce usages such as `DigitalSignature`, `KeyEncipherment`, `CertSign`, `CRLSign`, `ClientAuth`, `ServerAuth` or `OCSPSigning`."},"1920":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#key-usage-and-extended-key-usage","content":"If you enable **Honor Key Usage** or **Honor Extended Key Usages**, Lamassu keeps the values requested by the CSR. If you disable them, it replaces them with the ones defined in the profile."},"1921":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#key-usage-and-extended-key-usage","content":"Do not enable the `Honor…` options for untrusted requests unless another component validates those fields. Otherwise, the requester may choose broader capabilities than intended."},"1922":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#subject","content":"With **Honor Subject**, the certificate keeps the subject of the CSR. Without that option, Lamassu applies the profile's `CN`, `O`, `OU`, `C`, `ST` and `L`. If the profile does not define a `Common Name`, the requested CN is kept."},"1923":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#csr-extensions","content":"With **Honor Extensions**, Lamassu filters the additional requested extensions and keeps only SAN. Without that option, it discards the CSR's additional extensions."},"1924":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#csr-extensions","content":"This preserves SAN, but does not establish that the requester is entitled to those DNS names, IP addresses, emails or URIs. Validate that authorization before issuing. OCSP and CRL locations come from the issuance service configuration; `Honor Extensions` does not copy CSR distribution points."},"1925":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"The cryptographic enforcement can:"},"1926":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"allow or block RSA keys;"},"1927":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"limit the supported RSA sizes;"},"1928":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"allow or block ECDSA keys;"},"1929":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"limit the supported ECDSA sizes or curves."},"1930":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"When it is enabled, Lamassu checks the public key before creating a CA or signing a CSR. A key whose type or size is not listed in the profile is rejected."},"1931":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"Resolution depends on the entry point. One complete profile is selected; its fields are not merged with the CA’s profile."},"1932":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"Operation"},"1933":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"First choice"},"1934":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"Second choice"},"1935":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"If neither is supplied"},"1936":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"Direct signing with a CA"},"1937":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"`issuance_profile` embedded in the request"},"1938":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"Request `issuance_profile_id`"},"1939":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"CA default profile (`profile_id`)."},"1940":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"Issuance through a DMS"},"1941":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"`settings.issuance_profile_id`"},"1942":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"`settings.issuance_profile` embedded in the DMS"},"1943":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"Enrollment CA default profile."},"1944":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"If the selected identifier cannot be resolved, the operation fails; it does not silently fall back to the CA’s profile. Avoid setting both options at once. Recording which profile was selected helps explain why a certificate differs from its CSR."},"1945":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"Several fleets can share a CA while keeping different profiles through their DMSs. Requester authentication and device registration policy are configured separately in DMS."},"1946":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#define-a-single-purpose","content":"Separate, for example, mTLS devices, servers and intermediate CAs. A small, specific profile is easier to review than one that allows every use."},"1947":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#choose-the-validity","content":"Align the duration with the fleet's real renewal capacity. Leave margin against the CA's expiration."},"1948":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#fix-usages-and-subject","content":"For a device that authenticates as a client, the usual starting point is `DigitalSignature` and `ClientAuth`. Add `ServerAuth` or `KeyEncipherment` only if the protocol needs it."},"1949":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#constrain-the-keys","content":"Enable cryptographic enforcement and list only algorithms and sizes compatible with your policy and your devices."},"1950":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#attach-it-and-test","content":"Attach the profile to a CA or DMS and check the precedence above. Issue a CSR with known usages and SAN; inspect the result with `openssl x509 -in device.crt -noout -text`. Check subject, SAN, KU, EKU and dates. For an end-entity identity, disable `Sign as CA`, require no `CA:TRUE` or `Certificate Sign`, and require `CA:FALSE` if Basic Constraints is present."},"1951":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#attach-it-and-test","content":"Also try a key excluded by policy: issuance should fail. Follow the certificate verification and test acceptance in the intended consumer."},"1952":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#design-examples","content":"**mTLS device**\\\nEnd-entity certificate, short validity, `DigitalSignature`, `ClientAuth`, subject controlled by the DMS and SAN allowed when it identifies the device."},"1953":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#design-examples","content":"**TLS server**\\\nEnd-entity certificate, `DigitalSignature`, `ServerAuth` and mandatory SAN with the names clients will use."},"1954":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#design-examples","content":"**Intermediate CA**\\\n`Sign as CA`, `CertSign` and `CRLSign`, validity longer than its end-entity certificates and stricter cryptographic constraints."},"1955":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#design-examples","content":"These patterns express design decisions. Enabling `Honor Extensions` does not require a CSR to contain SAN or validate its names; enforce that in the request workflow. A profile does not install trust or grant permissions in the consumer."},"1956":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#changes-and-deletion","content":"Updating a profile affects future issuances; it does not modify already-signed certificates. Test changes before applying them to a CA in production and keep the operational justification."},"1957":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#changes-and-deletion","content":"Before deleting a profile, check that no CA or DMS depends on it. If you want to replace it, create the new version, update the references and perform a test issuance before retiring the old one."},"1958":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","type":"page","content":"Certificate validation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Validation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation"},"1959":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","content":"Check chain, identity, purpose and revocation from the consumer."},"1960":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Before querying status"},"1961":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"Choose a mechanism"},"1962":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#check-consumer-behavior","content":"Check consumer behavior"},"1963":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","content":"This guide brings together the checks needed when integrating a certificate consumer. You need the presented certificate, intermediates and roots that your application has deliberately chosen to trust. Lamassu publishes status; the consumer applies acceptance policy."},"1964":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Verify these criteria together:"},"1965":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Check"},"1966":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Required result"},"1967":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Chain and signature"},"1968":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Valid chain to a root deliberately installed in the consumer."},"1969":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Dates"},"1970":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Current time between `Not Before` and `Not After`, including the CAs in the chain."},"1971":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Identity"},"1972":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Name, SAN or identifier matches the expected peer."},"1973":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Purpose"},"1974":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"KU, EKU and constraints permit the specific operation."},"1975":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Revocation"},"1976":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Signed, current evidence corresponding to the queried issuer and certificate."},"1977":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"Authorization"},"1978":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"The application permits that identity to perform the action."},"1979":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#before-querying-status","content":"The issuance walkthrough checks chain and purpose with OpenSSL. That check does not automatically query OCSP or download a CRL. Inventory presence or an OCSP `Good` response does not replace the other criteria."},"1980":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"Mechanism"},"1981":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"When to use it"},"1982":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"What you must maintain"},"1983":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"OCSP"},"1984":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"Status query for a specific certificate."},"1985":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"Responder access, signature verification and cache/freshness policy."},"1986":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"CRL"},"1987":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"Local checks for many certificates or offline operation."},"1988":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"Periodic download of an issuer-signed list and rejection of expired lists."},"1989":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"OCSP can also return a response reusable until `nextUpdate`; a CRL changes when a new version is published. Neither mechanism alone guarantees that a consumer learns a revocation at the moment it is saved."},"1990":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"If using both, define when fallback is allowed and what the client does when retrieval, signature or freshness checks fail, or the result is `Unknown`. Accepting an identity when its status cannot be checked must be an explicit application decision."},"1991":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#check-consumer-behavior","content":"Accept a current, authorized certificate with a known chain."},"1992":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#check-consumer-behavior","content":"Reject another certificate with an unknown root or incompatible purpose."},"1993":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#check-consumer-behavior","content":"Revoke a test certificate and verify the OCSP response or new CRL."},"1994":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#check-consumer-behavior","content":"Check that a new connection with that identity is rejected."},"1995":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#check-consumer-behavior","content":"Simulate an unreachable endpoint and expired evidence; observe whether the result matches policy."},"1996":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#check-consumer-behavior","content":"Keep the serial number, issuer, revocation reason, query time and evidence timestamps. An existing session may need explicit closure or reauthentication in the consumer; publishing revocation does not automatically close it."},"1997":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#check-consumer-behavior","content":"For a chain with intermediates, validate their status according to consumer policy as well. An end-entity issuer’s CRL does not replace checks on every CA in the chain."},"1998":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#check-consumer-behavior","content":"<Card title=\"Online validation with OCSP\" description=\"Generate a query and verify signature, status and timestamps.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp\" />"},"1999":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificate-validation#check-consumer-behavior","content":"<Card title=\"Revocation lists\" description=\"Download, inspect and use an issuer’s CRL.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/crl\" />"},"2000":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","type":"page","content":"Certificates","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Keys, authorities and certificates"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates"},"2001":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","content":"Inspect, download and revoke the certificates issued by Lamassu."},"2002":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Find a certificate"},"2003":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#download-the-certificate","content":"Download the certificate"},"2004":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#issue-from-an-existing-csr","content":"Issue from an existing CSR"},"2005":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#revoke-a-certificate","content":"Revoke a certificate"},"2006":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#open-the-action","content":"Open the action"},"2007":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#choose-a-reason","content":"Choose a reason"},"2008":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#confirm-and-verify","content":"Confirm and verify"},"2009":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#reactivate-a-hold","content":"Reactivate a hold"},"2010":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#continue","content":"Continue"},"2011":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","content":"This guide is for a PKI operator inspecting or retiring an issued identity. You need inventory access and, to change states, permissions on the certificate. Open **Certificates** for a global view or **Issued Certificates** within a CA to restrict it to that issuer."},"2012":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Filter by `Common Name`, serial, status and issuer. A certificate does not contain its private key, so the private-key surfaces answer which certificates have their key held in Lamassu’s KMS:"},"2013":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"The advanced **Private Key** filter, available on the Certificates page and on a CA’s **Issued Certificates** tab, narrows the list to **All Certificates**, **With Private Key** or **Without Private Key**."},"2014":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"The sortable **Private Key** column — shown by default, hidden on narrow screens — marks a key held in the KMS with a green check mark and otherwise shows `-`."},"2015":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"In certificate details, the **Information** tab shows a **Private Key** row in the **Key & Signature** section. When the certificate reports a private key and its KMS engine and key IDs are available, the row links to the key (tooltip: **Open private key in KMS**). Otherwise, it shows **Present** if the certificate reports a private key, or **Not available** if it does not. This does not establish whether a key exists outside Lamassu."},"2016":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Use **Quick Inspect** for a quick review or **View Details** for subject, SAN, usages, chain, dates and metadata."},"2017":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Certificate records expose `key_id` (the KMS key that holds the private key, empty when the KMS does not hold it) and `has_private_key` (derived at read time from the KMS). Certificate and CA listings accept a `has_private_key` filter, which is useful, for example, to check the result of the CA-to-KMS migration of the 4.0.0 upgrade."},"2018":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Identify a certificate by issuer and serial; a name can correspond to several renewals. Check which certificate the consumer actually uses and which occupies the device’s active identity. Identity history and the certificate inventory answer different questions."},"2019":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#download-the-certificate","content":"Download the PEM and inspect it:"},"2020":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#download-the-certificate","content":"Check issuance policy, chain and usages with the verification walkthrough. A certificate does not contain its private key. For an external CSR, the key remains where it was generated; for the browser flow, retain the file downloaded upon issuance. If the key is lost, plan a new identity rather than expecting recovery from the certificate."},"2021":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#issue-from-an-existing-csr","content":"Use this flow when the identity’s key must remain on the system that generated it. You need an active CA with a usable key, a PEM CSR and a suitable profile."},"2022":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#issue-from-an-existing-csr","content":"Verify the request with `openssl req -in request.csr -noout -verify -text`. Review subject, SAN and algorithm, and authorize the requested identity."},"2023":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#issue-from-an-existing-csr","content":"Start issuance from the CA or inventory and select **Upload Existing CSR**."},"2024":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#issue-from-an-existing-csr","content":"Confirm the CA and profile resolved according to Profiles; the request does not guarantee that every field is retained."},"2025":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#issue-from-an-existing-csr","content":"Download the certificate and inspect dates, issuer, subject, SAN, KU and EKU. Check correspondence with the private key on the originating system."},"2026":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#issue-from-an-existing-csr","content":"Install certificate and chain in the intended consumer and test a connection. Issuance alone does not register a device or grant access in an integration."},"2027":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#issue-from-an-existing-csr","content":"For browser key generation, follow Issue your first certificate."},"2028":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#revoke-a-certificate","content":"Revoke when the key is compromised, the subject is no longer authorized or the identity must stop being accepted before expiration. Before changing status, identify consumers and prepare any required replacement."},"2029":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#open-the-action","content":"Locate the correct issuer and serial and select **Revoke Certificate**. A walkthrough is available in Revoke a certificate and check the CRL. `EXPIRED` records and records revoked for a final reason reject subsequent status changes."},"2030":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#choose-a-reason","content":"Select the incident reason. `CertificateHold` represents a reversible certificate suspension; other reasons block later changes. Do not use a suspension to address a compromised key."},"2031":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#confirm-and-verify","content":"Save the change and read the record again: require **REVOKED**, reason and timestamp. Then verify a fresh OCSP query and, if using CRL, its published version and the serial’s presence. Finally check rejection of a new connection in the consumer."},"2032":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#confirm-and-verify","content":"Revocation does not erase the certificate, delete the key or guarantee closure of existing sessions. Status and publication are separate steps."},"2033":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#confirm-and-verify","content":"A certificate revoked with `CertificateHold` can be reactivated if it is not in `EXPIRED` state. Its dates and consumer trust remain mandatory."},"2034":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#reactivate-a-hold","content":"Check that the saved reason is `CertificateHold` and the identity still satisfies policy. Request `ACTIVE` through the status update operation exposed by your installation; consult the API reference. Do not assume changing consumer permissions also changes status in Lamassu."},"2035":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#reactivate-a-hold","content":"Read the record and query OCSP again. With `regenerate_on_revoke` enabled, the reactivation event requests CRL regeneration: check that the new list omits the serial. An earlier list can still mark it revoked until the client refreshes its copy."},"2036":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#reactivate-a-hold","content":"This does not undo permanent revocation or a cascade started by revoking a CA."},"2037":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#continue","content":"<Card title=\"Validate with OCSP\" description=\"Query and verify a certificate’s signed status.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp\" />"},"2038":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/certificates#continue","content":"<Card title=\"Distribute a CRL\" description=\"Publish status for local validation.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/crl\" />"},"2039":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"page","content":"Certificate lifecycle","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle"},"2040":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","content":"Issuance, use, renewal, revocation and retirement of certificates in Lamassu."},"2041":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#the-full-journey","content":"The full journey"},"2042":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#request","content":"Request"},"2043":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#issuance","content":"Issuance"},"2044":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#use-and-monitoring","content":"Use and monitoring"},"2045":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-or-re-enrollment","content":"Renewal or re-enrollment"},"2046":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#revocation-or-retirement","content":"Revocation or retirement"},"2047":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"Certificate states"},"2048":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-and-revocation-are-not-equivalent","content":"Renewal and revocation are not equivalent"},"2049":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Effect of revoking a CA"},"2050":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"What you should watch"},"2051":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","content":"Issuing a certificate is only the beginning. During its useful life you must check its validity, renew it before it expires and retire it when it stops being trustworthy. Lamassu keeps the certificate, its issuing CA, its status and, when it belongs to a device, the identity it is linked to."},"2052":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#request","content":"The requester generates a key and a CSR. In the recommended flows, the private key stays in the device, browser or cryptographic engine that created it."},"2053":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#issuance","content":"The CA signs the CSR. The issuance profile determines the validity, uses, subject, allowed extensions and cryptographic constraints."},"2054":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#use-and-monitoring","content":"The certificate enters the `ACTIVE` state. Lamassu monitors its `Not After` date; the cryptographic monitoring job marks certificates that have expired as `EXPIRED`."},"2055":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-or-re-enrollment","content":"A new certificate is issued before the previous one expires. In a DMS you can open preventive and critical windows so the device re-enrolls through EST."},"2056":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#revocation-or-retirement","content":"If the identity stops being trustworthy, Lamassu records the reason and time of revocation. OCSP and CRLs let consumers learn that status."},"2057":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"Lamassu persists four X.509 states:"},"2058":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"**`ACTIVE`**: the record is enabled. Also check `Not Before` and `Not After`: this state does not establish time validity."},"2059":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"**`EXPIRED`**: it has passed its expiration date. The monitor detects this periodically; it is not a state that should be assigned manually."},"2060":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"**`REVOKED`**: it was invalidated before expiring, with a reason and a timestamp."},"2061":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"**`INACTIVE`**: it is disabled without representing a definitive revocation."},"2062":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"The device view may add operational states such as missing identity, pending renewal, expiring soon or decommissioned. These are an interpretation of the device's status and its certificates, not new X.509 states."},"2063":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-and-revocation-are-not-equivalent","content":"**Renewal** creates a successor certificate for an identity that remains valid. **Revocation** communicates that the current certificate must no longer be accepted. Renew to maintain continuity; revoke in response to compromise, retirement or a change that invalidates the identity."},"2064":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-and-revocation-are-not-equivalent","content":"Only `CertificateHold` allows reactivating a revoked certificate that is not in `EXPIRED` state. Revocation for another reason blocks subsequent status changes. `EXPIRED` records also reject changes; the consumer must check dates even before the monitor updates the state. Certificates explains how to verify revocation and reactivation."},"2065":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-and-revocation-are-not-equivalent","content":"The **Reissue CA** operation generates another certificate for the same key and links both serial numbers through metadata. It is not a key rotation. To change the key, create a successor CA and perform a migration with an overlapping period."},"2066":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Revoking a CA starts a cascade that attempts to revoke descendants with `CessationOfOperation`. It may end with partial failures and is not undone by reactivating the parent. Read Hierarchy and rotation for conditions and checks."},"2067":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Before confirming:"},"2068":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Identify DMSs, devices and services that trust that chain."},"2069":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Distribute the new chain of trust."},"2070":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Reissue the necessary identities."},"2071":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Check OCSP and CRL from a real consumer."},"2072":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Revoke the old CA once no legitimate traffic remains."},"2073":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Device retirement belongs to the IoT Fleets lifecycle. It affects the active identity; it does not automatically traverse and revoke every historical certificate. Review previous identities and consumer permissions separately in Device management."},"2074":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"Certificates entering the preventive or critical renewal window."},"2075":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"Repeated enrollment or re-enrollment failures."},"2076":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"Status changes and revocation reasons."},"2077":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"OCSP and CRL publication and validity."},"2078":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"Dependencies still presenting a replaced certificate."},"2079":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"The device history relates its previous and current identities. For administrative changes and mutation errors, see Audit logs."},"2080":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"page","content":"Trust model","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model"},"2081":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","content":"Understand where trust originates, how it is distributed and what each component validates."},"2082":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#the-four-trust-decisions","content":"The four trust decisions"},"2083":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#who-can-issue","content":"Who can issue"},"2084":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#what-can-be-issued","content":"What can be issued"},"2085":{"id":"