":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","content":"Revoke a certificate among many issued by a CA and confirm that its CRL lists it."},"2615":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"2616":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#revoke-the-certificate","content":"Revoke the certificate"},"2617":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#find-the-certificate","content":"Find the certificate"},"2618":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#revoke-it","content":"Revoke it"},"2619":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#confirm-and-read-the-status","content":"Confirm and read the status"},"2620":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#download-the-certificate","content":"Download the certificate"},"2621":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#check-the-crl","content":"Check the CRL"},"2622":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#verify-with-the-list","content":"Verify with the list"},"2623":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"If the result fails"},"2624":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","content":"You will revoke the certificate of `device-042`, one of the 100 certificates issued by the CA, and then check that the CA's revocation list (CRL) includes it while the other certificates remain valid. The result is a revoked certificate in Lamassu and a downloaded CRL that names its serial number and reason."},"2625":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"A CA with issued certificates and permission to change their status. The example uses `Acme Showcase Root CA` from Create your first CA, with the 100 client certificates `device-001` to `device-100`. A smaller set works the same way."},"2626":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"The CA's public certificate in `ca.pem`, as saved in the first path."},"2627":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"OpenSSL 3.x and `curl` on a computer that can reach the CRL endpoint."},"2628":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"Only `CertificateHold` can be undone later. Any other reason is final, so use an evaluation certificate for this path. Before revoking in production, identify the consumers of the identity and prepare a replacement."},"2629":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#revoke-the-certificate","content":"Follow the interactive walkthrough. It opens the issuing CA, filters its **Issued Certificates** by Common Name to find `device-042` among the 100, and revokes it with the reason `KeyCompromise`."},"2630":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#revoke-the-certificate","content":"In the console, the steps are:"},"2631":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#find-the-certificate","content":"Open **Certification Authorities**, select the issuing CA and go to **Issued Certificates**. Search by `Common Name` for `device-042`. The CA's own certificate is also listed in this tab; do not confuse the two."},"2632":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#revoke-it","content":"Open the **More actions** menu of the matching row and select **Revoke Certificate**. In the confirmation dialog, choose the **Revocation Reason** that describes the incident. This example uses `KeyCompromise`, because the device key is considered exposed. Use `CertificateHold` only for a reversible suspension."},"2633":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#confirm-and-read-the-status","content":"Select **Confirm Revocation**. The row changes to `REVOKED` and shows the reason and the revocation time. If you need to verify the result later, read the record again rather than trusting the dialog."},"2634":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#confirm-and-read-the-status","content":"Revocation does not delete the certificate or its key, and it does not close sessions that are already established. See Certificates for the reasons and their consequences."},"2635":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#download-the-certificate","content":"From the same **More actions** menu, select **Download PEM** and save the file as `device-042.crt`. Note its serial number and the CRL distribution point (CDP) it carries:"},"2636":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#download-the-certificate","content":"The URL ends with the ID of the **issuing CA**, not the ID or serial of the certificate. Your serial number differs from the one shown."},"2637":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#check-the-crl","content":"Lamassu regenerates the CA's CRL when a certificate is revoked, provided `regenerate_on_revoke` is enabled; it is by default. The endpoint is public and does not require authentication. Replace the URL with the CDP of your certificate and download the list:"},"2638":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#check-the-crl","content":"Check that the list is signed by your CA, is current and contains the serial number:"},"2639":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#check-the-crl","content":"Expect `verify OK`, the expected issuer, a `lastUpdate` not earlier than the revocation and an entry for the serial of `device-042` with reason `Key Compromise`; the list also names any other certificate previously revoked by this CA. A CRL with the same number as before the revocation means it has not been regenerated yet."},"2640":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#verify-with-the-list","content":"`openssl verify` can apply the downloaded list to a certificate. The revoked certificate must be rejected and any other certificate from the same CA must still pass. For `device-001`, download its PEM in the same way and save it as `device-001.crt`:"},"2641":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#verify-with-the-list","content":"This check uses your local copy of the list: it does not download newer lists or prove that every client has refreshed its copy. For online status, see OCSP."},"2642":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"Result"},"2643":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"What to review"},"2644":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"**Revoke Certificate** is not available"},"2645":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"The certificate is already `REVOKED` for a final reason or is `EXPIRED`."},"2646":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"The CRL download returns 404"},"2647":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"The ID in the URL is not the issuing CA's: use the CDP of the certificate."},"2648":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"`verify OK` fails"},"2649":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"`ca.pem` is not the certificate of the CA that signed the list."},"2650":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"The serial is not in the list"},"2651":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"The list was downloaded before the revocation, or its regeneration failed. See CRL settings errors."},"2652":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"`device-001` is also rejected"},"2653":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"The certificate was revoked, or `ca.pem` does not match its issuer."},"2654":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"<Card title=\"Manage certificates\" description=\"Reasons, holds and reactivation.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/certificates\" />"},"2655":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"<Card title=\"Revocation lists (CRL)\" description=\"Settings, regeneration and publication.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/crl\" />"},"2656":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/quickstarts/revoke-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"<Card title=\"Validate with OCSP\" description=\"Query the signed status of a certificate.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp\" />"},"2657":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"PKI troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Troubleshooting"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting"},"2658":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","content":"Diagnose certificate issuance, OCSP and CRL."},"2659":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Issuance fails"},"2660":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"OCSP or CRL do not reflect a change"},"2661":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#the-chain-validates-but-the-connection-fails","content":"The chain validates but the connection fails"},"2662":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","content":"This guide helps a PKI operator locate issuance and status publication failures. Keep the Lamassu version, operation, CA, issuer, serial, time and returned error. Do not include private keys or tokens in diagnostics."},"2663":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","content":"For Gateway, sign-in, pods, dependencies and messaging, see Deployment troubleshooting. For device enrollment, see EST diagnostics."},"2664":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Check"},"2665":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"What to inspect"},"2666":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Next step"},"2667":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"CA"},"2668":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Exists, is active and has usable dates."},"2669":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Authorities."},"2670":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Key"},"2671":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"The record has a usable private key and the engine can sign."},"2672":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Try **Sign / Verify** in KMS; check provider permissions and availability."},"2673":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"CSR"},"2674":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Correct PEM and verifiable signature."},"2675":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"`openssl req -in request.csr -noout -verify -text`."},"2676":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Profile"},"2677":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Selected source, existing ID, allowed algorithm and size."},"2678":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Check Profiles precedence; CA and DMS resolve differently."},"2679":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Result"},"2680":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Appropriate subject, SAN, usages and dates."},"2681":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Compare CSR, profile and certificate; successful issuance does not establish consumer acceptance."},"2682":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"For unexpected certificate fields, review `Honor Subject`, `Honor Key Usage`, `Honor Extended Key Usages` and `Honor Extensions`. The latter preserves SAN only, without validating entitlement to those names. Validity is not automatically clamped to CA expiration."},"2683":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"For CA reissuance failures, check revocation and date: reissuance is not supported for a revoked or already expired CA. To change its key, use Hierarchy and rotation."},"2684":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"Check each boundary independently:"},"2685":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Record:** read the correct certificate again by serial and issuer. Confirm status, reason and time; expired or permanently revoked records reject further transitions."},"2686":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Endpoint:** inspect AIA and CDP. Query those URLs from the consumer’s network; an old route or incorrect issuer can explain a discrepancy."},"2687":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**OCSP:** save a fresh response, verify signature and timestamps, and observe status. An HTTP error for an absent serial does not mean `Good` or guarantee a signed `Unknown`."},"2688":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**CRL:** compare `latest_crl`, number and timestamps with the downloaded list. Check the serial in its contents. If unchanged, review `regenerate_on_revoke`, event delivery, jobs, signing and storage with the deployment operator."},"2689":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Client:** check cache, policy for expired or unavailable evidence, critical IDP extension and rejection of a new connection."},"2690":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"Reactivation from `CertificateHold` needs a new CRL for the client to stop seeing the hold. Reactivating a CA does not restore its descendant cascade; inspect every status and individual operation failure."},"2691":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#the-chain-validates-but-the-connection-fails","content":"Check expected identity, SAN, KU/EKU, matching key, presented intermediates and consumer permissions. Distinguish server TLS trust, client authentication and action authorization. Follow Validation for positive and rejection tests."},"2692":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/platform/pki/troubleshooting#the-chain-validates-but-the-connection-fails","content":"When escalating a problem, provide identifiers, error and relevant public evidence, including query timestamps and version. This distinguishes issuance, publication and consumer application failures."},"2693":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","type":"page","content":"Security","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security"},"2694":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","content":"How to report a security vulnerability in Lamassu privately, what to include in a report and which releases receive security fixes."},"2695":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"Report a vulnerability"},"2696":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#what-to-include-in-a-report","content":"What to include in a report"},"2697":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#supported-versions","content":"Supported versions"},"2698":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#responsible-disclosure","content":"Responsible disclosure"},"2699":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","content":"Found a security vulnerability in lamassuiot, lamassu-dashboard, or lamassu-helm? This page explains how to report it privately, what to include in your report and which releases receive security fixes."},"2700":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"Do not report security vulnerabilities through public GitHub issues, discussions, or pull requests. Public reports disclose the problem before maintainers can fix it."},"2701":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"Instead, report privately using GitHub Security Advisories for the affected repository:"},"2702":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"lamassuiot"},"2703":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"lamassu-dashboard"},"2704":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"lamassu-helm"},"2705":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"This lets maintainers assess and address the issue before it is publicly disclosed."},"2706":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"If private vulnerability reporting is not enabled for that repository, report the vulnerability privately to lamassuiot\\@lksnext.com before disclosing any details publicly."},"2707":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#what-to-include-in-a-report","content":"Describe the vulnerability, its potential impact, and steps to reproduce it using non-sensitive, redacted examples."},"2708":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#what-to-include-in-a-report","content":"Do not include in the report:"},"2709":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#what-to-include-in-a-report","content":"Credentials, tokens, or private keys"},"2710":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-61/security#what-to-include-in-a-repor