abases or schemas, or a schema migration aborted: on duplicate CA IDs or missing `engine_id` values, or in the VA schema on a CA ID containing `/`, an SKI shared by more than one CA (the error asks you to recreate all but one of them on a different key), a role whose signer certificate has no key, a CA ID reserved for the archived settings of another role, or a CA ID equal to another role's SKI. The abort message names the offending objects; fix them and re-run the upgrade."],[3012,"**The VA migration fails with `cannot resolve signer certificate for VA role ... N candidates`.** The migration cannot uniquely identify a signer certificate from the SKI stored on the role. Review the SKI and candidate certificates reported in the error; correct the pre-migration data with a verified backup and rerun the migration. The new `signer_serial_number` field is created during that migration, so it cannot be set through the VA API while the migration is failing."],[686,"**TLS is always verified.** The receiver certificate is checked against the system trust store. `insecure_skip_verify` is enforced as `false` — including when it is set to `true` — so self-signed or otherwise untrusted receivers fail delivery."],[1953,"**TLS server**\\\nEnd-entity certificate, `DigitalSignature`, `ServerAuth` and mandatory SAN with the names clients will use."],[3028,"**Trust set.** `est_rfc7030_settings.client_certificate_settings.validation_cas` holds the expected CAs, in particular those of the old CA during rotation overlaps."],[2350,"**Type**: algorithm and key size, for example RSA 2048 or EC P-256."],[1886,"**Upload Existing CSR** is the right option when the key must remain on the target system. Lamassu receives the request but never the private key."],[780,"**Validation Authority (VA).** Publishes the status of certificates through OCSP and CRL."],[2176,"**Validation CAs:** authenticate the client certificates used for enrollment or migration. During re-enrollment, the enrollment CA is 