$.data` selects the event's `data` field, and the expression must start with `$`."],[2502,"the consumer applies revocation checks and authorization."],[2104,"The consumer keeps its own trust store. EST `/cacerts` can distribute the service TLS certificate, the enrollment CA and selected managed CAs. Initial trust for authenticating that service must come from an already trusted channel. Download and inspect the contents: do not assume they form a complete chain or install every entry as a root."],[753,"the consumer persists it exactly once;"],[2131,"The consumer trusts roots A and B, locally or through a trust authority managing the list."],[1074,"The consumer validates and authorizes the identity; the client schedules renewal and recovery."],[1742,"The consumer validates the identity and applies its access permissions."],[1056,"The controller also adds `Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64` to the outer header, although the outer body is MIME text. &#x2A;*Do not Base64-decode the entire body.** Read the actual boundary and decode each part according to its headers."],[628,"The credential could be processed but did not produce a positive authorization. Review in this order:"],[2292,"The CRL does not change after revoking a certificate."],[2646,"The CRL download returns 404"],[1881,"The CRL linked to the authority."],[2206,"The CRL settings of a CA store the configuration and metadata of its latest published list. Each CA has its own settings, keyed by its CA ID — even when two CAs share a key: they share the SKI, not the CRL. Generation requires a usable issuer key; do not assume an imported CA without a key has an available CRL."],[1925,"The cryptographic enforcement can:"],[2326,"The Cryptographic Key Management Service (KMS) of Lamassu IoT centralizes the generation, import, custody and use of the platform's keys. This is where you manage the keys that support the CAs and the rest of the signing operations that depend on the PKI."],[517,"The decision is made **befor